    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/professor-or-advanced-associate-professor-of-school-mental-health-and-the-science-of-learning-and-development-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Professor or Advanced Associate Professor of School Mental Health and the Science of Learning and Development",
      "description": "Professor or Advanced Associate Professor of School Mental Health and the Science of Learning and Development - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Professor or Advanced Associate Professor of School Mental Health and the Science of Learning and Development - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Professor or Advanced Associate Professor of School Mental Health and the Science of Learning and Development 45002649 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Faculty Administrator Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Education MBU Advertising Summary: The Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Education (SOE) is seeking a preeminent scholar who works at the intersection of child development, school mental health, implementation science, and machine learning (transcending at least two of these areas) with an August 10, 2027 start date (negotiable). Unit: School Of Education MBU Department: SOE Deans Office Deans Suite Duties & Responsibilities: At VCU, we provide UNcommon learning, research, creativity, service and discovery — the hallmarks of the VCU experience. A premier, urban, public research university nationally recognized as one of the best employers. VCU is a great place to work. It is a place of opportunity, where your success is supported and your career can thrive. VCU offers employees a generous leave package, career paths for advancement, competitive pay, and an opportunity to do mission-driven work At VCU, we believe that bringing different perspectives, expertise, experiences, and approaches together strengthens research, teaching, and solutions to complex problems. This philosophy drives our recruitment process, so we welcome applicants whose scholarship, teaching, professional experiences, and collaborative work contribute to a supportive and intellectually vibrant community of faculty, staff, and students. The SOE’s commitment to responsive, needs-driven and research-based educational practices that transform lives aligns with One VCU Research’s overarching mission to enrich the human experience, advance societal wellbeing, and optimize health through transdisciplinary, collaborative research. By grounding educational inquiry in evidence-based, community-focused research and leveraging cross-disciplinary partnerships, SOE faculty contribute directly to One VCU’s strategic priorities of innovation, social impact, and transformative change across health, education, and social domains. The SOE recognizes that educational, developmental, and mental health outcomes are shaped by individual, cultural, institutional, and contextual factors and values scholarship that examines how these factors influence access, engagement, implementation, and outcomes across populations and settings. Furthermore, our faculty within the SOE and affiliated centers (e.g., Partnership for People with Disabilities; Research, Rehabilitation and Training Center) conduct federally funded, impactful research that contributes to University Research Clusters, including Pedagogy, Learning and Community Advancement; Neuroscience, Pain, Addiction and Mental Health; Children and Women’s Health and Wellbeing; AI, Quantum Technologies and Data Science; and Robotics, Machine Learning and Virtual Reality. The current faculty search, which leverages our Culture of Collaboration, prioritizes a nationally/internationally renowned scholar with expertise and funding that transcends at least two of the following areas that align with both the One VCU Priorities and the University Research Clusters: the Science of Learning and Individual Development (SOLID), School Mental Health, Implementation Science and/or Machine Learning. Applicants with exceptionally strong records of research, teaching and leadership work experience within interdisciplinary teams are encouraged to apply. Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. An earned doctorate in education or related field closely related to SOLID, school mental health, implementation science and/or machine learning. A distinguished record of teaching, scholarship, and professional service commensurate with tenure at the rank of advanced associate or full professor at a research-intensive university. A well-developed scholarly/research portfolio appropriate to complement existing expertise in the SOE. A scholarly record that demonstrates sustained impact via high quality publications. A track record of securing external funding to support research. Record of effective leadership and capacity to promote a strong collegial culture and climate. Demonstrated ability to conduct and/or translate research that is responsive to the needs and experiences of varied populations and contexts, with attention to access, implementation, engagement, or outcomes. Ability to develop and support collaborative relationships across the university and community, including school systems, state agencies, research institutes, and policy networks. Preferred Qualifications: Experience leading or partnering with large center grant proposals Evidence of collaborations with research centers, institutes and/or community agencies/organizations Evidence of service and leadership in national or international professional associations Evidence of interdisciplinary collaboration in research program Experience working effectively across cultural, disciplinary, institutional, and community contexts. Benefits : All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. Salary Range: $180,000-260,000 Rank: Open FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Hours per Week: 1 Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Hybrid Tenure: Tenure Track Months: 9 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Dr. Kevin Sutherland Contact Email: kssuther@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 90dac9cb Last Name (required) 386b385f Email (required) 284e0807 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 6663174e First Name (required) 7f2532f6 Last Name (required) f9bd97d3 Email (required) aae29017 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 03382e75 Last Name (required) f3350bfd Email (required) 192bd6a0 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along with third party non-persistent and persistent cookies to collect non-identifiable data from site visitors. VCU uses this collected data to prioritize and improve the content it delivers to its site visitors and to promote the university in a manner that is most relevant to its site visitors. I do not accept I accept"
