    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/assistant-professor-of-management-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Management - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor of Management - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor of Management 45002609 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Faculty Administrator Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Business MBU The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship in the School of Business at Virginia Commonwealth University invites applicants for two full-time tenure track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin August 2027 . For the first faculty position, we seek candidates with teaching interests in strategic management and research interests in strategic management and/or entrepreneurship. Primary teaching responsibilities include our undergraduate strategic management capstone course, with additional teaching possible at the MBA or doctoral level. The second position is open regarding teaching and research interests. Welcome to VCU where we don't just prepare for the future - we build it. As one of the nation's most innovative public R1 research universities, VCU brings together learning, discovery, creativity, service, and impact in ways few institutions can match. Located in the heart of Richmond, Virginia, VCU is a premier urban research university where bold ideas are encouraged, disciplinary boundaries are crossed, and ambitious scholars find the resources and community to turn vision into reality. At VCU, you will join a community that embraces excellence, rewards innovation, and supports ambitious ideas. Your success will be backed by meaningful institutional investment, competitive compensation, strong benefits, and supportive, motivated colleagues. We value differing perspectives and believe the most significant breakthroughs happen when talented people come together around a shared purpose. The VCU School of Business The Management and Entrepreneurship Department is housed in the VCU School of Business , which advances research that shapes new thinking in business and policy. Scholars here thrive in an environment that values high-impact research, innovative teaching, and cross-disciplinary collaboration and are supported by strong industry partnerships and robust research resources. Offering bachelor's, master's, certificate and doctoral programs, the School ranks among the top six percent of business schools worldwide. Nearly 4,000 students each year gain the knowledge, skills and experience to succeed in a rapidly changing business environment, and leading national employers actively recruit VCU Business graduates. The School's location in Virginia's capital connects faculty to a vibrant ecosystem of corporations, startups, nonprofits, healthcare organizations and government agencies that create rich opportunities for research, partnership and impact. This isn't business as usual. It's innovation at work. In the Management and Entrepreneurship Department , we offer an undergraduate major in Management with concentrations in business administration, entrepreneurship, and international business; an undergraduate major in Human Resource Management; and a Ph.D. in Business. Management faculty teach in the undergraduate, MBA, Executive MBA, and Ph.D. programs. The Department has 14 full-time faculty who are active researchers and engaged teachers. Our faculty have publications in leading journals including Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice, Journal of Applied Psychology, Journal of Business Venturing, Journal of Management, Organization Science, Organizational Research Methods, Personnel Psychology, Psychological Bulletin, and Strategic Management Journal. The city of Richmond consistently ranks among “Best Places to Live and Work in America” in several national publications and has received numerous accolades for its vibrant food and craft beer offerings and its outdoor and arts scenes. The School of Business at Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is fully accredited by the AACSB and is housed in a state-of-the-art facility, Snead Hall. Since its founding in 1937, the School of Business has built strong ties with the Richmond community and beyond. Offering 13 bachelor’s and 19 master’s degrees, as well as the Ph.D. in Business, we welcome nearly 4,000 students each year. Our programs develop skills that result in highly sought-after graduates with many national corporations identifying VCU’s School of Business as a target school for recruitment. Responsibilities: This first Assistant Professor position is responsible for teaching interests in strategic management and research interests in strategic management and/or entrepreneurship. Primary teaching responsibilities include our undergraduate strategic management capstone course, with additional teaching possible at the MBA or doctoral level. The second position is open regarding teaching and research interests. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Candidates should have a doctorate in management or a closely related field from an AACSB accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered if the degree will be completed prior to start date. Experience leading classroom learning; one anticipated curriculum area is strategic management while a second area is open. An established research agenda as well as potential for scholarship to complement and expand existing expertise in the department. Demonstrated experience working in and fostering an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from various backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications Candidates should have the ability to publish in top-tier peer reviewed academic journals and have an active research agenda. We seek candidates who have good communication skills, demonstrated commitment to excellence in both teaching and research, and a desire to work collaboratively with colleagues. Prior industry work experience is beneficial. Salary Range: $165,000-180,000 Application Process: Candidates should upload: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and the names and e-mail addresses of four references through the VCU Jobs website. Reference letters will be requested by the search committee only for the short-listed candidates. Only complete applications that meet the required qualifications will be considered. For additional information, please contact search committee chair Dr. Blakley Davis: bcdavis@vcu.edu . Priority consideration will be given to applications received by January 4, 2027. Additional Information: Benefits : All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Hybrid Rank: Assistant Professor Tenure: Tenure Track Months: 9 months Contact Information Contact Name: Dr. Blakley Davis Contact Email: bcdavis@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) c80390e9 Last Name (required) 8baa2fa8 Email (required) f492e70b Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out