    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/open-rank-faculty-social-and-behavioral-sciences-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states-806c8dfd-68c8-4ae2-a7cc-dae29d92b7bf": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty - Social and Behavioral Sciences",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty - Social and Behavioral Sciences - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Open Rank Faculty - Social and Behavioral Sciences - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Open Rank Faculty - Social and Behavioral Sciences 45002604 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School of Public Health MBU Mission or Goal of Unit: In the Department of Social and Behavioral Sciences (SBS) we strive for optimal health for all people via research, education, and service, with community engagement at the heart of all we do. Our work spans the translational continuum within public health, focusing on understanding and transforming the systemic, structural, social, and behavioral factors that affect health to promote well-being for all. Housed within the R1 Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Public Health (SOPH), the SBS Department is home to 13 full-time faculty and a robust funding portfolio that exceeded $2.67M in expenditures in FY 2026. Areas of existing research strength within SBS include: prevention and management of chronic diseases; health disparities and health equity; cancer prevention and control; health communication; and women’s health. Equally central to our purpose is our educational mission—our SBS educational programs include a PhD in Social and Behavioral Sciences and an MD-PhD, both of which center community engagement and experiential learning. We aim to prepare scholars to work across disciplines and in partnership with both organizations and local communities in service of real-world public health impact. We also contribute teaching, leadership and mentorship for our MPH program and growing BSPH. In particular, SBS faculty developed and teach many core courses for the Cancer Prevention and Control Sciences and Health Communication concentrations for the MPH degree. For more details, please visit http://www.sbs.vcu.edu . Purpose of this position: The Department of Social and Behavioral Sciences in the Virginia Commonwealth University School of Public Health invites applications for a full-time 12-month, tenure-eligible, open rank faculty member. We are seeking experienced scholars with a commitment to our tripartite mission across scholarship, teaching, and service. Applicants with formal training and methodological expertise in behavioral clinical trials, intervention science, and community-engaged research are particularly of interest. We welcome applications from scholars who conduct community-grounded work focused on cancer disparities, rural health, chronic disease prevention and management, or other areas that complement existing strengths in the unit and School. Those applying at the assistant professor level should show evidence of research productivity and strong potential to obtain external funding. Applicants at the associate professor or full professor level should show evidence of a well-developed research portfolio including multidisciplinary projects and extramural funding commensurate with rank. Tenured and tenure-eligible faculty are generally expected to support at least 50% of their effort via grants. Position Responsibilities: Research: The faculty member is expected to build and maintain an independent, programmatic line of research in behavioral interventions, and/or community-engaged research in an area that complements and/or augments existing strengths in the unit. A combination of extramural funding as PI and collaborator that aligns with our unit’s mission, vision, and values is expected. Teaching: The faculty member will also support the department with teaching responsibilities aligned with their expertise and across levels (i.e., PhD, MPH, BSPH). Candidates will also mentor scholars in our PhD program. Service: The faculty member is expected to serve on Departmental, School, and/or University committees as necessary, as well as in a professional capacity in their discipline (e.g., reviewer, conference organizer, etc.). Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant health-related field (e.g., social and behavioral sciences, public health, psychology) Expertise in behavioral clinical trials, intervention science, and / or community engaged research Advanced expertise in research design and methodology Proven record of peer-reviewed publications and evidence of or commitment to lay data dissemination Strong track record of—or significant potential for—securing extramural funding Ability to work independently and collaboratively and commitment to strong departmental citizenship Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral research training experience Teaching experience at the graduate or undergraduate level Experience in mentorship of graduate students Formal training in community-based participatory research Required Materials: Review of applications will begin November 11, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should submit the following materials and an official application. Brief cover letter detailing interest in this specific position, and highlighting alignment between the SBS Department, VCU, and their interests and expertise CV Research statement (no more than 2 pages) Teaching and mentorship statement (no more than 2 pages) Salary Range: Commensurate Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Open Tenure: Tenure Track Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Cian Brooks Contact Email: Brookst10@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 640d4a7f Last Name (required) 51f4c173 Email (required) af5da7e8 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 26714a97 First Name (required) d580a242 Last Name (required) 2becbd7e Email (required) 3d0aca3d Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 28dbb9eb Last Name (required) 6d4ba21e Email (required) 7048337d Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-pe