    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/director-of-cardiovascular-nutrition-research-internal-medicine-cardiology-phc-f80500-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Cardiovascular Nutrition Research - Internal Medicine, Cardiology (PHC) - F80500",
      "description": "Director of Cardiovascular Nutrition Research - Internal Medicine, Cardiology (PHC) - F80500 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Director of Cardiovascular Nutrition Research - Internal Medicine, Cardiology (PHC) - F80500 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director of Cardiovascular Nutrition Research - Internal Medicine, Cardiology (PHC) - F80500 45002434 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School of Medicine Department: Internal Medicine Mission of the Unit/Department: Today, early career scientists in multi-disciplinary translational cardiovascular research are needed to improve diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of cardiovascular disease (CVD). CVD burden has been rising for decades in most countries and the age-standardized rate of CVD has also risen in locations where it had been previously declining (including central Virginia and many other regions in the United States). Concurrently, the CVD workforce in the United States has been shrinking—including MD and PhD investigators who are trained in multidisciplinary CVD research and how to pursue solutions that would reduce the national and global CVD burden. The goals of the Division of Cardiology and the Pauley Heart Center are thus to attract and train a cohort of outstanding academic scientists in multidisciplinary translational CV research, and build a robust training infrastructure to increase the number of scientists trained to conduct research to advance the treatment and prevention of CVD. Duties & Responsibilities: The Pauley Heart Center in concert with the Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Cardiology are seeking extramurally-funded, accomplished, early-career investigators to pursue funded research opportunities for the purpose of reducing the burden of CV disease. Teaching Perform teaching responsibilities related to undergraduate, graduate and early career investigators seeking research opportunities involving CV medicine Research Conduct research at the interface of cardiometabolic disease and noninvasive imaging, focusing on the early detection of subclinical processes Work with center director and computer science team to incorporate artificial intelligence (AI) tools to enhance imaging workflows and streamline data processing and interpretation Perform image analysis and support research in both preclinical (animal) and human subject studies, assisting collaborating investigators (faculty and trainees) with image data interpretation and reporting Conduct cardiometabolic molecular experiments independently in preclinical cardiovascular science laboratory and through utilization of institutional metabolomic core laboratories; analyze and report results; perform statistical analyses in collaboration with center statisticians Write scientific manuscripts and seek independent funding through submission of grant proposals Collaborate closely with faculty, fellows, and technical staff to support ongoing research and educational missions Present findings at internal meetings and contribute to external publications and conference abstracts Service Serve on Pauley Heart Center Review Committees for Pilot programs Support & Educate Trainees involved in CV research Serve on Institutional Review Board Committee assignments Other Supervise Staff involved in Grant preparation activities Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Ph.D., M.D./Ph.D., or equivalent in cardiovascular science, or a related discipline Experience with noninvasive imaging modalities (MRI) in clinical or research settings Strong foundation in cardiometabolic disease mechanisms and subclinical disease pathways Experience working in both preclinical and clinical research environments Demonstrated ability to conduct and interpret statistical analyses relevant to biomedical research Familiarity with image processing software and interest in developing or applying AI/machine learning tools Excellent organizational and communication skills; ability to work collaboratively across clinical and basic science teams Strong scientific writing skills with experience preparing manuscripts or grant proposals Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Research experience in areas of diet, activity, behavioral interventions Salary Range: Commensurate Benefits: All full-time university faculty are eligible for VCU's robust benefits package, that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted: No ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Clare Greene Contact Email: Clare.Greene@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 0e3c926b Last Name (required) c23ffa88 Email (required) 50b5283d Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: cd02e663 First Name (required) 87926691 Last Name (required) 4172a81e Email (required) a64a8e75 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 6212fafc Last Name (required) 188acb2f Email (required) 2f6f4db0 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discard