    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/bsw-msw-on-campus-instructor-school-of-social-work-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "BSW/MSW ON-CAMPUS Instructor- School of Social Work",
      "description": "BSW/MSW ON-CAMPUS Instructor- School of Social Work - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States BSW/MSW ON-CAMPUS Instructor- School of Social Work - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search BSW/MSW ON-CAMPUS Instructor- School of Social Work 45002466 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Academic and Faculty Affairs Faculty Adjunct School Of Social Work MBU Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is seeking qualified candidates for an On-Campus Adjunct Faculty position in Social Work within the School of Social Work. This position offers opportunities to teach in the on-campus modalities of the Bachelor of Social Work (BSW) and Master of Social Work (MSW) programs, across a variety of subjects, including: human behavior in the social environment, research, generalist/clinical/macro practice, policy, social justice, and various elective topics. BSW/MSW ONCAMPUS Instructor Position Responsibilities for Community Embedded Teaching: ● Deliver high-quality instruction during weekly in-person classes on the Richmond, VA campus ● Utilize VCU’s learning management system, Canvas ●Prepare weekly lesson plans to facilitate effective learning experiences ●Hold weekly office hours to provide guidance and support to students ●Engage with students in a timely manner, utilizing excellent written and oral communication skills ●Provide feedback and grades to students promptly ●Fulfill additional duties as required while teaching in our Programs ●Adhere to all Virginia Commonwealth University and School of Social Work policies ● Other duties as assigned ● Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU This is a part-time, non-benefited appointment Salary: $4,626 (3 credits) $1,542 per credit hour Application Process: To apply for this position, please submit the following documents along with answers to the questions in the application: ● A cover letter expressing your subject-matter expertise and your qualifications for teaching (required) ● Current curriculum vitae (CV) highlighting relevant educational and professional experiences (required) ● Contact information for two professional references (required) ● Clinical licensure (if applicable) Please note the following details: ● Your application will become part of the Talent pool, which will be accessed only when an opening arises. If a suitable opening becomes available, we will review your qualifications ● Please be aware that we are unable to hire applicants who are not already in the Talent pool Required Qualifications: ● A minimum of a Master's degree in Social Work or a related field ● Demonstrated expertise and experience in the field of social work or a related field- two years post-graduate degree is preferred ● Teaching experience, preferably in higher education, with a focus on social work education or a related field ● Strong interpersonal and communication skills ● Clinical licensure is required for certain courses ● Commitment to adhering to Virginia Commonwealth University and School of Social Work policies ● Commitment to adhering to the NASW Code of Ethics Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) c96f9246 Last Name (required) 8b46dabe Email (required) 84612527 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to so