    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-and-director-dental-hygiene-school-of-dentistry-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate / Professor and Director - Dental Hygiene - School of Dentistry",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate / Professor and Director - Dental Hygiene - School of Dentistry - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Assistant / Associate / Professor and Director - Dental Hygiene - School of Dentistry - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant / Associate / Professor and Director - Dental Hygiene - School of Dentistry 45002477 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Health Sciences Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Dentistry MBU Unit: School of Dentistry Department: General Practice Duties & Responsibilities: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Dentistry is seeking applicants for a full-time faculty position in the Department of General Practice, Division of Dental Hygiene. Academic rank, tenure eligibility, and salary commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Mission or Goal of Unit: The primary mission of the School of Dentistry is to educate practitioners of Dentistry capable of meeting the general oral health needs of the communities they serve. Integral parts of the mission are research and other scholarly activity, patient care, leadership in dental education and organized dentistry, and collaboration and participation with other units within VCU and VCU Health System. As the only dental hygiene program located within a dental school in the Commonwealth of Virginia, our students have a unique opportunity to work in integrated clinical settings alongside DDS students as well as with faculty members from Dental Hygiene, dentistry and specialty areas. The Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Dentistry is located in downtown Richmond, Virginia. With a 133-year history, Virginia’s only dental school offers opportunities for selected, qualified individuals to study dentistry and oral health through its Doctor of Dental Surgery (D.D.S.) program, graduate specialty training programs, and a dental hygiene program. The VCU School of Dentistry is one of a small number of dental schools in the country affiliated with an academic medical center, the only dental school in the Commonwealth, and one of the oldest dental schools in the United States, founded in 1893. It is one of six health sciences academic programs on the Medical College of Virginia (MCV) Campus of VCU. Position Responsibilities: The VCU School of Dentistry, Department of General Practice is seeking a full-time Faculty to fill the position of Director for the Dental Hygiene Program. The purpose of this position is to inspire student success, provide strong academic leadership, promote innovation and faculty achievement, and foster educational inclusiveness. The Dental Hygiene Program Director is directly responsible and accountable for ensuring the fulfillment of educational goals and objectives, ensuring program compliance through accreditation by the Committee on Dental Accreditation (CODA). In addition, the Dental Hygiene Program director holds the authority and responsibility for all administrative functions of the program as well as supervision of program faculty and students in a collaborative environment. The Dental Hygiene Program Director serves as a liaison with the administration of the School of Dentistry and reports directly to the Department Chair. The program director is also responsible for didactic, preclinical and clinical instruction of undergraduate and pre-doctoral students and participates in student advising, committee assignments, and scholarly activities. The Dental Hygiene Program Director serves as the Chair of Dental Hygiene Admissions, facilitating recruitment and retention of a varied student body. Additional responsibilities include providing continuing education offerings to healthcare professionals. The Program Director will strive for excellence in educating a varied student population prepared to promote optimum oral health in the community. Core Responsibilities and Administrative Duties: Coordinate program assessment activities on an annual basis Faculty supervision - Directs the coordination, and recruitment of faculty including faculty schedules, teaching assignments and evaluation Curriculum - provides leadership for program curriculum development, evaluation and revision to ensure student success Assess program mission and goals, ensuring alignment with school and university strategic plans Assessing, planning and operating program administration. Initiate faculty development Prepare faculty contracts Chair the dental hygiene admissions committee-coordination, evaluation and participation in determining admission criteria and procedures as well as student promotion and retention criteria Maintain quality assurance to remain compliance with all required agencies, including the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) Maintain communication and work cooperatively with the department chair and Dean of the school Serve as representative on school and university committees Coordinate budgets and program instructional needs and supplies with the department chair Schedule and conduct program meetings Serve as an academic advisor Serve as course director and provide clinical instruction, maintaining syllabi, grading and the electronic management system Serve as chair of the dental hygiene class committee and a liaison to the Academic Progress Committee Maintain program website and university bulletin Required Qualifications: Masters degree or higher in dental hygiene education or a related field Graduate of a program accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation Eligible for licensure in Virginia Certification in local anesthesia and nitrous oxide/oxygen sedation Current CPR certification Minimum of one year of clinical experience as a hygienist Didactic teaching experience Excellent interpersonal skills and communication skills A demonstrated potential for leadership Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU For tenure-eligible positions at the Assistant Professor rank, an established research agenda and a clear potential for external funding, as well as potential for scholarship or creative expression to complement and expand existing expertise in the department For tenure-eligible positions at the Associate Professor or Professor ranks, a well-developed scholarly/research portfolio with evidence of multi-disciplinary applications and external funding appropriate to complement and expand existing expertise in the department Preferred Qualifications: A minimum of three (3) years' experience in college level teaching is preferred Completion of a formalized leadership program is preferred Three recent letters of reference, or contact information for at least three references, will be required for consideration. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Salary Range: Commensurate Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Fully Onsite Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Michelle McGregor Contact Email: mrmcgregor@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) b83df3f6 Last Name (required) 81fd1472 Email (required) 42a65167 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 9204961d First Name (required) dfad322a Last Name (required) 39a917b1 Email (required) bc454389 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 8dc4c653 Last Name (required) 02d0e9d7 Email (required) 954b02a6 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement