    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/director-transgenic-and-knockout-mouse-core-facility-faculty-cellular-molecular-and-genetic-medicine-som-f80540-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Director, Transgenic and Knockout Mouse Core Facility Faculty - Cellular, Molecular and Genetic Medicine-SOM-F80540",
      "description": "Director, Transgenic and Knockout Mouse Core Facility Faculty - Cellular, Molecular and Genetic Medicine-SOM-F80540 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Director, Transgenic and Knockout Mouse Core Facility Faculty - Cellular, Molecular and Genetic Medicine-SOM-F80540 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director, Transgenic and Knockout Mouse Core Facility Faculty - Cellular, Molecular and Genetic Medicine-SOM-F80540 45002401 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Research Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School of Medicine Department: Cellular, Molecular and Genetic Medicine Department Summary: The Department of Cellular, Molecular and Genetic Medicine is dedicated to unraveling the fundamental biology that supports health and drives disease. Our faculty, trainees and students tackle some of the most pressing challenges in biomedical science, from the molecular and genetic roots of disease to the complexities of whole-body physiology. Our foundational studies are driving the frontiers of scientific discovery, pushing the boundaries of what we understand about biology, disease and the human body. From our labs in downtown Richmond to research collaborations around the world, our work is generating new knowledge, influencing the direction of biological science and redefining what is possible in biomedical research. We are proud to be a community of passionate educators and mentors, deeply committed to empowering the next generation of scientists and leaders. With alumni enjoying successful careers across a broad spectrum of industries, our rigorous training programs offer students a transformative education that drives innovation today and creates lasting impact for tomorrow. Position Overview: We are seeking a highly motivated scientist to lead animal model creation at a large (>$500M in research awards) Carnegie R1 research university. This is an exciting opportunity to work with a highly respected and experienced team with a long history of serving the university’s research community. The Director must possess comprehensive knowledge of all aspects of the Core’s operations. This role supports a varied active user base across VCU—predominantly within the School of Medicine (SOM), but also servicing the School of Pharmacy, School of Dentistry, and others, as well as external investigators. The Director ensures the seamless delivery of major core services, including breeding colony management (the facility's largest service line), cryopreservation, rederivation/IVF, and the production of new genetically engineered mouse models (GEMMs). Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Scientific & Operational Direction Core Oversight: Prioritize and supervise all daily technical functions, project timelines, and operational workflows within the Core; management of three direct reports Investigator Consultation: Meet with faculty and investigators to discuss new projects, design custom genetic strategies, and provide regular status updates on ongoing projects Institutional Grant Support: Provide customized letters of support for faculty grant submissions, assist investigators with budget preparation, and directly participate in grant and manuscript writing Importation & Logistics: Collaborate with the Division of Animal Resources (DAR) to manage mouse line importation and rederivation. Assist investigators with identification of existing mouse models and with the logistics for procurement from sources such as the Mutant Mouse Resource and Research Center (MMRRC) and various international sources of mouse lines Specialized Grant Leadership: Serve formally as the Director of the Mouse Core for key institutional research grants Technical Innovation: Keep the facility at the cutting edge of genome-editing capabilities by tracking emerging methodologies and staying active within professional networks such as the International Society for Transgenic Technologies (ISTT) Institutional Engagement: Attend and contribute to relevant Massey Comprehensive Cancer Center meetings, including Scientific Steering Committee meetings and External Advisory Board meetings, ensuring alignment of Core activities with institutional priorities and strategic goals 2. Administrative & Financial Leadership Regulatory Compliance: Serve as the Principal Investigator (PI) on two Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) protocols and maintain compliance as the PI on the Virginia Board of Pharmacy license Grant Reporting: Support institutional grant mechanisms by managing deliverables for the Massey Comprehensive Cancer Center Support Grant (CCSG), including compiling annual progress reports and driving the 5-year renewal process Financial Oversight: Direct budgeting and financial cost accounting, including the annual A21 cost accounting processes and monthly financial dashboard certifications Complex Billing Management: Oversee and execute the Core's multi-stream billing framework 3. Teaching & Mentorship Responsibilities Didactic Instruction: Develop and deliver formal lectures on genetically modified mice in several university courses (e.g., “Techniques in Molecular Biology and Genetics”) Specialized Training: Provide ad-hoc lectures focused on operational best practices in Mouse Breeding Colony Management Hands-on Mentorship: Provide direct, one-on-one scientific and technical training to graduate students, postdocs, and laboratory trainees utilizing the Core's services Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Advanced scientific degree (preferably Ph.D.) in genetics, molecular biology, or a related biomedical field Deep, comprehensive scientific and technical expertise across all facets of GEMM technologies Proven administrative capacity to manage complex budgets, multi-user facility operations, and institutional compliance protocols Excellent communication skills Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Prior direct experience managing or directing a successful Transgenic and Knockout Core Facility or similar shared resource lab Demonstrated record of collaborative grant writing and peer-reviewed publications Salary Range: Commensurate Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU's robust benefits package, that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No Sensitive Position: Yes ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Other Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Email: SOMHR@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 77542487 Last Name (required) fd4fff0c Email (required) 1c3150f4 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 8c0205c5 First Name (required) 28aecf7e Last Name (required) 22d82ba9 Email (required) 9feab243 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) b8223e12 Last Name (required) 1f11be7a Email (required) 92d27595 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along with third party non-persistent and persiste