    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/som-musculoskeletal-radiologist-radiology-m89965-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "SOM Musculoskeletal Radiologist (Radiology M89965)",
      "description": "SOM Musculoskeletal Radiologist (Radiology M89965) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States SOM Musculoskeletal Radiologist (Radiology M89965) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search SOM Musculoskeletal Radiologist (Radiology M89965) 45002628 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Health Sciences Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU's sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Radiology Duties & Responsibilities: To provide specialized musculoskeletal imaging interpretation and interventions, with the use of state-of-the-art equipment. This full-time musculoskeletal radiology position will include training residents and fellows within an academic radiology department. Clinical: Provide high quality subspecialized musculoskeletal imaging interpretations in support of the referring physicians and patients of VCUHS. Responsibilities will include interpretations of musculoskeletal radiology images (radiographs, US, CT, MR) and performing musculoskeletal interventions. Teaching: Provide training to medical students, residents, and fellows that rotate through the Department of Radiology Research: Professional relationships established with the Department of Orthopedic Surgery to foster interdisciplinary research Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respected, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff or students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Applicants should be ABR certified or have passed the Core Component of the ABR Board Examination Fellowship training in Musculoskeletal Imaging Candidates must be eligible for a Virginia medical license Candidates must be eligible for permanent employment in the USA Preferred Qualifications Interest in performing interventional procedures Interest in clinical research Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Mary Ann Turner, MD Contact Email: mary.turner@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 87bed71d Last Name (required) 9a3bd93d Email (required) 29cd53af Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 7d3de7db First Name (required) 5a2e1841 Last Name (required) f4d290c1 Email (required) 8097eaf0 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, 