    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/assistant-professor-of-accounting-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Accounting - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor of Accounting - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor of Accounting 45002608 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Business MBU Welcome to VCU where we don't just prepare for the future - we build it. As one of the nation's most innovative public R1 research universities, VCU brings together learning, discovery, creativity, service, and impact in ways few institutions can match. Located in the heart of Richmond, Virginia, VCU is a premier urban research university where bold ideas are encouraged, disciplinary boundaries are crossed, and ambitious scholars find the resources and community to turn vision into reality. At VCU, you will join a community that embraces excellence, rewards innovation, and supports ambitious ideas. Your success will be backed by meaningful institutional investment, competitive compensation, strong benefits, and supportive, motivated colleagues. We value differing perspectives and believe the most significant breakthroughs happen when talented people come together around a shared purpose. The VCU School of Business The Accounting Department is housed in the VCU School of Business , which advances research that shapes new thinking in business and policy. Scholars here thrive in an environment that values high-impact research, innovative teaching, and cross-disciplinary collaboration and are supported by strong industry partnerships and robust research resources. Offering bachelor's, master's, certificate and doctoral programs, the School ranks among the top six percent of business schools worldwide. Nearly 4,000 students each year gain the knowledge, skills and experience to succeed in a rapidly changing business environment, and leading national employers actively recruit VCU Business graduates. The School's location in Virginia's capital connects faculty to a vibrant ecosystem of corporations, startups, nonprofits, healthcare organizations and government agencies that create rich opportunities for research, partnership and impact. This isn't business as usual. It's innovation at work. The Department of Accounting is inviting applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. We invite you to join our collaborative group of accomplished and innovative accounting faculty. Duties & Responsibilities: Assistant professors support the missions of the department of accounting and the School of Business by conducting research, teaching, and service activities. We welcome applications from candidates across all research and teaching specialty areas. Teaching responsibilities for this position will be primarily in face-to-face classroom settings. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Must possess a PhD in Accounting or be an accounting doctoral candidate with PhD degree completion expected by August 2027. Excellent oral and written English language skills Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated ability to conduct and publish high-quality academic research. A demonstrated ability to teach effectively in a higher education setting. Professional work experience in an accounting or finance role. Salary Range: $195,000-215,000 Application Process: Candidates should upload: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and the names and e-mail addresses of four references. Reference letters will be requested by the search committee only for the short-listed candidates. Only complete applications that meet the required qualifications will be considered. Review of applications will start immediately, and will continue until filled. Priority consideration will be given to applications received before November 8, 2026. For additional information, please contact search committee chair Jean Zhang at jxzhang@vcu.edu Additional Information: Benefits : All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid leave and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Assistant Professor Tenure: Tenure Track Months: 9 months Contact Information Contact Name: Jean Zhang Contact Email: jxzhang@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 6b7abd3d Last Name (required) 0a8f7343 Email (required) c05c11c4 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: cefd1533 First Name (required) 25475e98 Last Name (required) 571abfcb Email (required) e20a84e3 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you