    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/allergist-internal-medicine-rheumatology-m89685-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Allergist - Internal Medicine, Rheumatology - M89685",
      "description": "Allergist - Internal Medicine, Rheumatology - M89685 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Allergist - Internal Medicine, Rheumatology - M89685 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Allergist - Internal Medicine, Rheumatology - M89685 45002571 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Department: Internal Medicine Position Summary The Division of Rheumatology, Allergy and Immunology at Virginia Commonwealth University is searching for a full-time Adult Allergy and Immunology physician to participate in clinical, teaching and research activities. Providers will see Patients at the Adult Outpatient Pavilion in Downtown Richmond, VA. Successful applicants will be board certified or board eligible in Allergy/Immunology and will be expected to provide quality and timely clinical care on the inpatient and outpatient unit. The ideal candidate must be able to develop an academic career focused primarily on patient care, but also involving teaching and clinical research as well as participation in our ACGME -accredited program in Allergy and Immunology Mission or goal of the unit: The Virginia Commonwealth University Health System programs in Rheumatology and in Allergy and Immunology are among the oldest clinical in the USA. This unit comprises a combined division with allergy/immunology and rheumatology sections working towards the goal of improving outcomes for patients with autoimmune, musculoskeletal, allergic, mast cell, eosinophil and primary immune deficiency disorders through clinical care, research, and public service, including philanthropy. Chief purpose of this position: The chief purpose of this position is to advance the patient care, research and teaching missions of Allergy and Immunology through direct patient care in the hospital / clinic and training of residents, medical students and other trainees on in support of above mission or goal Duties & Responsibilities: Clinical (100%) Provide excellent patient care in Adult Allergy and Immunology and focused areas of interest and experience in outpatient settings. Actively participate in management of patients on Adult AI consult service Other (for instance administrative duties, etc.) Comply promptly with billing, documentation, credentialing and other administrative requirements of the department Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Qualified applicants for this position should have demonstrated both scholarly and clinical abilities through patient care teaching and clinical research. Candidates should be Board-certified in Allergy, Immunology, and in Internal Medicine. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Flexible Work Arrangement: Other Restricted: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Shannon Sekerak Contact Email: Shannon.Sekerak@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 11a3c19a Last Name (required) 47ae1cfa Email (required) 1d736d29 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge th