    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/assistant-associate-dean-for-faculty-affairs-development-dean-s-office-school-of-dentistry-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs & Development - Dean's Office - School of Dentistry",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs & Development - Dean's Office - School of Dentistry - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Assistant / Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs & Development - Dean's Office - School of Dentistry - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant / Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs & Development - Dean's Office - School of Dentistry 45002540 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Health Sciences Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Dentistry MBU Advertising Summary: VCU School of Dentistry invites applications for the position of Assistant / Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs and Development. As Virginia’s only dental school, VCU advances education, research, and patient care while shaping the next generation of dental leaders. Qualified candidates committed to fostering an exceptional academic environment are encouraged to apply. Unit: School of Dentistry Department: Dean's Office Department Summary: The Virginia Commonwealth University’s (VCU) School of Dentistry advances oral health through education, research, patient care, and leadership. As part of Virginia’s only dental school—founded in 1893 and affiliated with an academic medical center—it contributes to a long tradition of excellence in dental education and health sciences. Duties & Responsibilities: The Assistant / Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs and Development provides leadership, oversight, and strategic direction for faculty‑related programs, policies, and initiatives within the Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Dentistry. This position supports faculty onboarding, appointment, evaluation, promotion and tenure, development, and engagement, ensuring alignment with VCU policies, accreditation standards, and the School’s mission. The Assistant / Associate Dean works collaboratively with department chairs, faculty, Human Resources, and senior leadership to foster an equitable, supportive, and high‑performing academic environment. This position reports to the Dean of the School of Dentistry and collaborates directly with department chairs, Human Resources, Academic Affairs, Clinical Affairs, and University Administration and Faculty Affairs offices. The Assistant / Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs and Development plays a critical role in cultivating a thriving academic community. By supporting faculty affairs, development, recognition, and retention, this position strengthens the School’s teaching, research, and clinical missions and ensures a supportive, equitable, and forward‑looking faculty culture. The Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Dentistry is located in downtown Richmond, Virginia. With a 133-year history, Virginia’s only dental school provides opportunities for selected, qualified individuals to study dentistry and oral health through a Doctor of Dental Surgery (D.D.S) program, graduate specialty training programs and a dental hygiene program. The VCU School of Dentistry is one of a small number of dental schools in the country affiliated with an academic medical center, the only dental school in the Commonwealth, and one of the oldest dental schools in the United States founded in 1893. It is one of six health sciences academic programs on the Medical College of Virginia (MCV) Campus of VCU. Position Responsibilities: Faculty Affairs Administration Manage and oversee faculty appointment, reappointment, promotion, and tenure processes in accordance with VCU policies and school bylaws and guidelines Maintain faculty policies, guidelines, and governance documents; ensure consistent interpretation and application across departments Oversee annual faculty evaluations, workload documentation, and performance improvement plans Serve as a primary resource for faculty regarding policies, career pathways, compliance, training and institutional expectations Faculty Onboarding, Promotion and Tenure Partner with department chairs to support faculty onboarding, retention strategies, position development, search processes, and succession planning Coordinate onboarding programs that introduce new faculty to academic policies, teaching expectations, clinical operations, training and school culture Manage and oversee the faculty promotion and tenure processes, consulting and guiding faculty through the process, ensuring compliance with University guidelines and procedures Support retention initiatives that strengthen faculty engagement and long‑term commitment to the VCU School of Dentistry Tenure Compliance, Credentialing, and Accreditation Ensure faculty‑related processes comply with the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) standards, VCU policies, and state/federal regulations Maintain accurate faculty credentialing records and support accreditation documentation related to faculty qualifications and development Coordinate with Academic Affairs, Human Resources, and Clinical Affairs to ensure faculty meet licensure, certification, and training requirements Strategic Leadership Serve as a member of the School’s leadership team and contribute to strategic planning, policy development, and organizational initiatives Chair or participate in committees related to faculty affairs, development, and academic governance Provide data‑driven insights on faculty demographics, workload, performance, and development needs Please Note: The position is a Teaching and Research Faculty role and may include responsibilities in instruction, scholarly activity, community service, and clinical practice, depending on the candidate's background, credentials, and training. The selected candidate will receive an academic appointment within the appropriate department of the School of Dentistry. Qualifications: Required Qualifications Master's degree or a terminal degree in a field directly related to academic administration Minimum of 3 – 5 years of experience in higher education, faculty affairs, faculty development or academic administration Demonstrated understanding of faculty development, academic policies, and promotion/tenure processes Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and institutional leadership Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU For tenure-eligible positions at the Assistant Professor rank, an established research agenda and a clear potential for external funding, as well as potential for scholarship or creative expression to complement and expand existing expertise in the department For tenure-eligible positions at the Associate Professor or Professor ranks, a well-developed scholarly/research portfolio with evidence of multi-disciplinary applications and external funding appropriate to complement and expand existing expertise in the department Preferred Qualifications PhD, EdD, DHSc, DDS / DMD, or equivalent terminal degree Experience in faculty affairs leadership within a dental or health‑related professional school Record of teaching excellence and familiarity with faculty development best practices Experience designing faculty development programs or mentoring initiatives Evidence of scholarly activity in dental education, leadership, or faculty development Additional Information: Three recent letters of reference, or contact information for at least three references, will be required for consideration. Salary Range: Commensurate Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Fully Onsite Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Dr. Oonagh Loughran Contact Email: oloughran@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 1e737677 Last Name (required) a875768f Email (required) 43f7019c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 19dc7643 First Name (required) 93f64b9e Last Name (required) 3212e21a Email (required) b0a4008d Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and