    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/assistant-professor-of-research-school-of-social-work-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Research - School of Social Work",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Research - School of Social Work - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor of Research - School of Social Work - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor of Research - School of Social Work 45002426 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Social Work MBU Virginia Commonwealth University's School of Social Work welcomes applications for an Assistant Professor of Research position with the Evaluation Lab, where community-engaged research, collaborative partnerships, and meaningful social impact come together. Position Overview The Evaluation Lab at the School of Social Work (SSW) at Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) provides research and evaluation services to SSW field agencies and community partners as well as nonprofit organizations, government agencies and a variety of other organizations. Our mission is to give back to our partners and work collaboratively to address their needs; we offer our research expertise while depending on knowledge, guidance and feedback from our partners throughout the research process. Our services include program evaluation, survey development and administration, grant writing, data analysis, research dissemination, and more. The Evaluation Lab is staffed with social work faculty and staff across a range of expertise and alongside graduate and undergraduate research assistants. For more information visit our website at https://socialwork.vcu.edu/uncommon-strengths/evaluation-lab/ . Founded in 1917, the VCU School of Social Work is a long-established leader in social work education and research. With BSW, MSW, and PhD programs, and both online and on-campus learning modalities, we are one of the largest accredited, comprehensive social work programs in the U.S. A preeminent urban public university and health sciences center, VCU is one of only 28 Carnegie-designated Research Intensive (R1) and Community Engaged public universities nationwide. VCU is located in the capital city of Richmond, recently ranked among the top 25 places to live in the U.S. Our proximity to the state capital facilitates collaboration with state and federal agencies and related organizations. Faculty maintain dynamic relationships with community agencies and research groups in the area and throughout the U.S. and the world. To learn more about the School of Social Work, please visit https://socialwork.vcu.edu/ . Key Responsibilities Key responsibilities of the Assistant Professor of Research include, but are not limited to: Collaborate closely with the Evaluation Lab on program planning, budgeting, research activities, and evaluation initiatives. Plan, coordinate, and facilitate Evaluation Lab meetings, activities, and project deliverables. Assist with the day-to-day coordination of graduate and undergraduate field placements and research training programs. Contribute to the development and implementation of research training curricula. Coordinate and oversee student recruitment, selection, placement, and training activities. Ensure the timely completion of required regulatory documentation and compliance processes. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students in research and evaluation activities, with an emphasis on community-engaged research, knowledge translation, and science communication. Pursue and contribute to scholarly activities, including publications, grant development, and teaching opportunities. Support and contribute to Evaluation Lab projects and initiatives as assigned by the Dean. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Doctorate in social work, psychology, behavioral sciences, or a related field. Experience with policy-related research, providing training and technical assistance to local and state organizations (e.g., development of training modules), and program evaluation, including conducting critical literature reviews, synthesizing community-level demographic and socioeconomic information, and developing policy recommendations. Experience working with foundations and engaging and collaborating with community stakeholders. Experience mentoring students at the undergraduate and graduate levels and developing research-focused training plans and curricula. Proficiency in computer applications, including statistical, data management, and word processing software (e.g., Google Workspace, Microsoft Office Suite, REDCap, SPSS, or R). Excellent oral and written communication skills. Excellent time management, organizational, and project management skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications MSW with clinical and/or community practice experience. Knowledge of, and/or established relationships with, local and state community agencies. Experience working in a fast-paced research environment. Familiarity with behavioral health research and community-engaged research. Experience teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students, including managing evaluation- or research-focused student field placements. Experience using administrative and research-related software applications, such as Collegiate Travel Planners, Chrome River, xTrain, and Articulate/Rise 360. Experience coordinating student travel and related logistics. Benefits : All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. Position Details Salary Range: $85,000 - $95,000 FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Hours per Week: 40 Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Hybrid Rank: Assistant Professor Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 Contact Information: Contact Name: Dr. Amy Adkins Contact Email: adkinsae@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 6362191c Last Name (required) 259e9078 Email (required) f1b3a54a Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 762567ff First Name (required) 3464cc13 Last Name (required) 4423724b Email (required) 5935714e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 1c94fbd4 Last Name (required) a1e8970b Email (required) 2415d620 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookie