    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/assistant-professor-school-of-medicine-neurosurgery-f80200-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, School of Medicine, Neurosurgery (F80200)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, School of Medicine, Neurosurgery (F80200) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor, School of Medicine, Neurosurgery (F80200) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor, School of Medicine, Neurosurgery (F80200) 45002407 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. https://vcujobs.com/why-richmond Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave granted up front, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. Unit: School of Medicine Department: Neurosurgery Mission or Goal of Unit: As clinicians, educators, and investigators in the evolving field of Neurosurgery, our mission is to improve the health of all people by excelling in patient care, education, and research. Chief Purpose of This Position: The Department of Neurosurgery is seeking candidates for a full-time faculty position as a Teaching and Research Faculty member within the department of Neurosurgery. The faculty member will conduct research, engage in medical student and neurosurgery resident and fellow education, and participate in clinical and/or translational research. Position Responsibilities: Teaching The faculty member will be expected to teach medical students, neurosurgery residents, along with those from other Departments, and fellows. Research The department is engaged in clinical and translational research projects. The faculty member will be expected to participate in, and when appropriate lead, clinical and/or translational research projects and clinical trials. The prospective candidate should be an accomplished neurobiologist interested in neurotrauma, pediatric neurobiology, and pediatric brain injury. The successful candidate will work closely with other researchers within the departments of Neurology, Pathology and Neurobiology and contribute to the research mission of the department of Neurosurgery by obtaining extramural funding, publishing peer-reviewed manuscripts, and conducting collaborative research. Service The faculty member will serve on departmental, School of Medicine, and/or University committees as necessary, as well as in a professional capacity in their field, e.g. reviewer, conference organizer, etc. Clinical None Minimum Qualifications: PhD degree (or equivalent) Minimum of two years of postdoctoral training experience Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU For tenure eligibility at the Assistant Professor rank, an established research agenda and a clear potential for external funding, as well as potential for scholarship or creative expression to complement and expand existing expertise in the department For tenure eligibility at the Associate Professor or Professor ranks, a well-developed scholarly/research portfolio with evidence of multi-disciplinary applications and external funding appropriate to complement and expand existing expertise in the department Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience in a university setting Published works on the field Strong analytical, observational, and problem-solving skills A good record of attending conferences and academic events Excellent research, writing including grants, and interpersonal skills A passion for teaching and engaging with students Salary Range: $90,000 - $110,000/annually FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Denise Mitchell Contact Email: denise.mitchell1@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) da137f0e Last Name (required) 26ef4378 Email (required) a4f1670e Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: d6531eb8 First Name (required) 85059075 Last Name (required) 5d9b5119 Email (required) 7be7c486 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology