    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/ob-gyn-combined-complex-family-planning-generalist-physician-obgyn-som-m89922-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "OB/GYN Combined Complex Family Planning/Generalist Physician | OBGYN | SOM |M89922",
      "description": "OB/GYN Combined Complex Family Planning/Generalist Physician | OBGYN | SOM |M89922 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States OB/GYN Combined Complex Family Planning/Generalist Physician | OBGYN | SOM |M89922 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search OB/GYN Combined Complex Family Planning/Generalist Physician | OBGYN | SOM |M89922 45002400 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: ObGyn Department Summary: The mission of the Obstetrics and Gynecology department is to provide the highest quality clinical care in both general and specialty Obstetrics and Gynecology to the women of the Commonwealth of Virginia. In addition to the clinical mission, the department has the allied goals of providing undergraduate and graduate medical education in the field and advancing the field through basic and clinical research. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is seeking qualified candidates to provide OB/GYN specialty and Complex Family Planning subspecialty care, including but not limited to early pregnancy failure, contraception, and family planning services. Complex Family Planning is currently an underserved clinical subspecialty in central Virginia and neighboring regions. The position will also include in- and outpatient consultation and performance of therapeutic procedures in the outpatient setting, the operating room, and possible consideration for off-site locations in collaboration with other clinics. This position will include participation in student and resident education as well as in the department’s clinical research Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching The faculty member will have teaching responsibilities to include actively participating in the department’s educational activities, with particular attention to educating students and residents in their core educational objectives in obstetrics, gynecology, and family planning. Research The person filling this position is encouraged to initiate clinical research projects. They are expected to participate in and facilitate other department research and contribute to scholarly publications/presentations. Service The faculty member will serve on departmental, health system, and university committees as necessary, as well as in a professional capacity in their field. The faculty member will be assigned to committees at the discretion of the division director and department chair. Clinical Full participation in the clinical activities of the complex family planning section is expected. Clinical activities are to be determined by the general obstetrics and gynecology division chief and complex family planning section chief and are expected to include a combination of clinic, inpatient care, surgery, and participation in nighttime call duties as appropriate. Other The faculty member will participate in department and institutional administrative activities as assigned by the division chief and/or department chair. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Eligible for medical license in Virginia Completion of training in Obstetrics and Gynecology equivalent to ACGME and ABOG accredited residency programs Completion of training in Complex Family Planning equivalent to ACGME accredited fellowship programs Potential for scholarship or creative expression to complement and expand existing expertise in the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications Completion of an ACGME accredited OB/GYN residency Demonstrated talent and experience in teaching and commitment to research, and patient care BC/BE by the American Board of OB/GYN in Obstetrics and Gynecology BC/BE by the American Board of OB/GYN in Complex Family Planning Salary Range: Commensurate with experience FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No RESTRICTED: No Flexible Work Arrangement: Other Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Name: Ashley Krauss Contact Email: ashley.krauss@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) c7ff23f4 Last Name (required) abe4b607 Email (required) 09a92d9d Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 9968a161 First Name (required) 863738a6 Last Name (required) 7db04dbb Email (required) 5ab63d93 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Resp