      "description": "Urologist | M68218 | Department of Urology - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Urologist | M68218 | Department of Urology - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Urologist | M68218 | Department of Urology 45002438 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Dorothy A Pauley Dept of Urology Department Summary: The mission the Department of Urology is the pursuit of excellence in all three areas of an academic surgical practice: teaching, research, and patient care. Duties & Responsibilities: The Department of Urology is recruiting an open rank, term, non-tenured track faculty position with a practice focused on general urology. The candidate will primarily provide clinical services at the Medical College of Virginia Hospital Campus located in Richmond, Virginia or its satellite affiliates. Services will include clinic, operative services, inpatient and consult management, teaching of residents, and call coverage. Teaching : The faculty member is expected to teach students and residents during the performance of daily clinical services. Formal teaching is required and includes the performance and/or oversight of resident didactics or grand rounds 1-2 times per year and in-person or virtual attendance of at least 60% of didactics and grand round sessions. Research : The faculty member is expected to participate in clinical trials or other research endeavors as available. Service : The faculty member is expected to serve on departmental and/or health system committees as necessary and to attend required faculty meetings. Clinical : The faculty member is expected to build and maintain a busy, patient centered clinical practice. This includes both inpatient and outpatient management of general urologic conditions including the provision of operative services. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Graduation from an ACGME accredited urology residency training program Board Certification or Eligibility in Urology Superior communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level Experience or interest in quality improvement Experience or interest in medical education Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No RESTRICTED: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Lisa Hook Contact Email: lisa.lomagliohook@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) c525d02e Last Name (required) e6bc00ce Email (required) 26b5612f Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 93967896 First Name (required) 419a2f5f Last Name (required) 67eb3ee1 Email (required) 7b8a6894 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through th