      "title": "Director of Quality and Safety, VAMC Liaison, and Faculty Leave Manager | M89524 | Department of Urology",
      "description": "Director of Quality and Safety, VAMC Liaison, and Faculty Leave Manager | M89524 | Department of Urology - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Director of Quality and Safety, VAMC Liaison, and Faculty Leave Manager | M89524 | Department of Urology - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director of Quality and Safety, VAMC Liaison, and Faculty Leave Manager | M89524 | Department of Urology 45002471 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Dorothy A Pauley Dept of Urology Duties & Responsibilities: Serve as the Quality & Safety faculty representative for the adult urology Faculty Serve on any relevant Department, Hospital, SOM, or University Quality & Safety committees Work with Urology Residency Program Director, Associate Program Directors, and Program Coordinators to develop yearly Quality and Safety Initiatives with Urology Faculty, Residents, APPs, and other clinical staff. Initiatives should follow the Plan-Do-Study-Act (PDSA) model and should be tracked with definable milestones. Serve as Faculty Liaison for the VAMC, including working with VCUHS and VAMC admin staff on onboarding new faculty and management of VAMC faculty call schedules Serve as the VAMC residency site director Oversee and manage the Adult Urology Faculty leave and call schedules Oversee and manage the Adult Urology Faculty Attending of the Day Schedules, including working to ensure daily and overnight consults are appropriately staffed and billed. Maintain required MCVP faculty privileges and required annual compliance and training Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications MD degree required. Demonstrated experience in residency training and medical education. Proven leadership experience in teaching residents across all levels of training, including delivering didactic lectures and supporting progressive leadership development throughout residency. Strong knowledge of ACGME Urology competencies and residency program requirements. Expertise in urological surgery, clinical procedures, and procedural training. Comprehensive knowledge of urological surgical and procedural equipment, including competency assessment and training. Ability to mentor, evaluate, and develop residents in both clinical and academic settings as they progress in their trainings. Excellent communication, teaching, and leadership skills with a commitment to advancing resident education and professional growth. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No RESTRICTED: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Email: SOMHR@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 272cdb80 Last Name (required) 9ccbb23a Email (required) 4d6f0dc2 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit informati