    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/transplant-nephrologist-internal-medicine-nephrology-m89923-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Transplant Nephrologist - Internal Medicine | Nephrology - M89923",
      "description": "Transplant Nephrologist - Internal Medicine | Nephrology - M89923 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Transplant Nephrologist - Internal Medicine | Nephrology - M89923 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Transplant Nephrologist - Internal Medicine | Nephrology - M89923 45002383 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Department: Internal Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: The Transplant Nephrologist will contribute to and enhance the educational and clinical activities of The Section of Transplant Nephrology within the division of Nephrology by providing compassionate, efficient, high quality consultative patient care in outpatient and inpatient settings and support the research goals of the division and department. Teaching: Teach fellows, residents and medical students using adult teaching methods that enhance and encourage active learning and ongoing professional development. Complete student, resident and fellows evaluations. Participate in other Nephrology educational activities including resident didactic series, conferences, morning report, Nephrology and Internal Medicine Grand Rounds, and other educational duties assigned by the department and service. Research: Participate in clinical and administrative research according to skills, interest and funding. Provide mentoring and supervision of fellows and residents in research and QI initiatives. Research opportunities may include performance improvement initiatives or formal extramurally funded investigations and participation may be as principal investigator or co-investigator. Service: Work with institutional and administrative staff to attain the objectives of Virginia Commonwealth University and VCU Health System including patient safety, patient satisfaction, maintenance and enhancement of public perception and fiscal health. Clinical: Provide excellent patient care in Transplant Nephrology and focused areas of interest and experience in both inpatient and outpatient settings. May also include coverage of General Nephrology as directed by Division Chief. Other (for instance administrative duties, etc.): Comply promptly with billing, documentation, credentialing and other administrative requirements of the department. Qualifications: Board certification or eligibility in Nephrology. Direct experience in managing complex inpatients and outpatients. Completion of accredited fellowship in general nephrology. Requires an interest in teaching and growth in an academic setting. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Restricted: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Rebecca Mullin Contact Email: Rebecca.Mullin@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 313289e2 Last Name (required) b67227eb Email (required) de10756e Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth 