    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/associate-dean-of-undergraduate-programs-and-department-chair-school-of-nursing-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states-f6f48539-802c-452e-8981-355d0da1d7d2": {
      "title": "Associate Dean of Undergraduate Programs and Department Chair – School of Nursing",
      "description": "Associate Dean of Undergraduate Programs and Department Chair – School of Nursing - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Associate Dean of Undergraduate Programs and Department Chair – School of Nursing - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Associate Dean of Undergraduate Programs and Department Chair – School of Nursing 45002402 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Nursing MBU Unit: School of Nursing Department: Family and Community Health Nursing Mission We champion health and well-being through the power of nursing education, discovery and practice. Role Purpose and Scope VCU School of Nursing invites candidates to apply to the Associate Dean of Undergraduate Programs and Department Chair position. This senior academic leader provides strategic, operational, and visionary oversight of all pre-licensure and undergraduate academic programs and the Department of Family and Child Health Nursing. This Associate Dean ensures academic excellence, program integrity, and curriculum alignment with the School’s mission and national and professional standards. The role oversees faculty orientation, development, mentoring, and workload planning; supports student success initiatives; manages clinical partnerships; and collaborates closely with School leadership to advance academic, research, practice, and community engagement priorities. The position works closely with the Dean, the Associate Dean for Graduate Programs, Associate Dean for Academic Affairs (ADAA), the Associate Dean for Research, Scholarship and Innovation (ADRSI), and the Associate Dean for Practice and Community Engagement (ADPCE) to support the School’s mission and facilitate communication across the organization. Core Leadership Responsibilities Fosters a positive work environment grounded in strong communication, collaboration, and consensus-building within the department and across the organization. Establishes program and department-related goals and initiatives that support the overall mission of the school and university. Provides guidance to program directors (PDs) to ensure academic integrity and teaching excellence within programs. Collaborates with the ADAA in preparation of internal and external administrative reports. Assists with the recruitment and retention of qualified faculty and staff. Leads organizational‑level orientation for new faculty and staff. Develops annual faculty work plans, including teaching assignments, for all faculty within the department. Evaluates staff, full-time faculty, part-time faculty, and adjunct faculty within the department (with input from the ADRSI, ADPCE, and PDs as appropriate). Mentors department faculty and ensures opportunities for faculty development. Addresses faculty, staff, and student matters within programs and the department in alignment with university and school policies. Manages program and department resources effectively to support operational excellence. Represents the department in interactions with university and community stakeholders as needed. Maintains teaching, research/ scholarship, and service responsibilities aligned with area of expertise and as outlined in agreement with the Dean. Required Background and Expertise Full-time senior faculty rank (Associate Professor or Professor) Currently licensed or eligible for licensure to practice nursing in Virginia, with a minimum of two years’ experience in direct clinical care Earned doctorate in nursing or related discipline (at least one graduate degree must be in nursing) Demonstrated teaching experience in nursing programs Demonstrated leadership and mentorship experience in academic programs Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Experience and Expertise Tenured or tenure-eligible Academic administrative experience History of external funding for research, scholarly, or academic projects Personal Characteristics Strong communicator with the ability to engage faculty, staff, students, and academic leaders Approachable and visible leader with an empowering, open‑door style Supportive of a broad range of experiences, ethical, and a trustworthy professional who models integrity and maturity Innovative and engaging leader who inspires respect, clarity, and enthusiasm Creative problem‑solver with initiative and adaptability in leading change Consensus builder and collaborative team player with strong follow‑through Organized and analytical with excellent time‑management and political acumen Salary Range: Commensurate with experience FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. Contact Information: Contact Name: Demmie Pennix and Terry Jones Contact Email: dpennix@vcu.edu and tjones69@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 83aa5660 Last Name (required) 7cbab5f0 Email (required) 6d65f3fb Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: d8cea897 First Name (required) 6ae88e2e Last Name (required) a91df43f Email (required) 4a8206f5 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 61c23e45 Last Name (required) 2848fc6a Email (required) 67dce1a0 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along with third party non-persistent and persistent cookies to collect non-identifiable data from site visitors. VCU uses this collected data to prioritize and improve the content it delivers to its site visitors and to promote the university in a manner that is most relevant to its site visitors. I do not accept I accept"
