    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/department-of-art-history-adjunct-instructor-vcuarts-qatar-qatar": {
      "title": "Department of Art History - Adjunct instructor - VCUarts Qatar - Qatar",
      "description": "Department of Art History - Adjunct instructor - VCUarts Qatar - Qatar Department of Art History - Adjunct instructor - VCUarts Qatar - Qatar Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Department of Art History - Adjunct instructor - VCUarts Qatar 45002478 Qatar Faculty Adjunct Qatar Campus MBU VCUarts Qatar invites applications for an adjunct faculty position to teach ARTH 103: Survey of Art I . This is a part-time adjunct appointment dependent on departmental needs. The Department of Art History seeks a dynamic and student-centered educator to teach an introductory survey course covering art from the prehistoric era through the 13th century. The course includes examples from selected regions of Europe, Asia, Africa, and the Americas, and introduces students to visual analysis and other art historical methods through illustrated lectures and discussion. Adjunct faculty are valued members of the academic environment at VCUarts Qatar and are expected to contribute to a collaborative, respectful, and learning-centered community of students, faculty, and staff. ARTH 103. Survey of Art I. 3 Hours. Semester course; 3 lecture hours, delivered online and face-to-face. 3 credits. This introductory survey of art examines artistic production from the prehistoric era through the 13th century, including examples from selected regions of Europe, Asia, Africa, and the Americas. Illustrated lectures demonstrate visual analysis and other art historical methods while identifying key monuments and artists’ work in relation to historical contexts. Key Responsibilities Teach ARTH 103: Survey of Art I in accordance with the approved course description, learning outcomes, and departmental expectations. Prepare and deliver lectures, readings, assignments, discussions, and assessments that support student learning. Introduce students to visual analysis, art historical methods, key monuments, artists, and historical contexts. Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. Maintain regular communication with students and the department regarding course expectations, progress, and academic matters. Maintain accurate records of attendance, grades, and student progress using university systems. Foster a respectful, professional, and intellectually engaging classroom environment. Adhere to departmental and university policies and procedures. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Art History or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated teaching experience at the university level or relevant professional experience in art history, museum studies, curatorial practice, or a related field. Strong written and verbal communication skills in English. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCUarts Qatar. Eligibility to work in Qatar or meet applicable immigration/employment requirements under Qatari law. Preferred Qualifications PhD in Art History or a closely related field. Previous experience teaching art history survey courses at the university level. Experience using learning management systems and educational technology. Experience teaching in international or multicultural higher education environments. Evidence of student-centered teaching practices. Application Materials Applicants must submit the following through the VCU Jobs website: Current CV/resume. Letter of interest outlining relevant teaching experience, professional background. List of three current references, including names, phone numbers, and email addresses. References will not be contacted without the applicant’s prior approval. Only applications submitted through the VCU Jobs website will be considered. Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 950f2d44 Last Name (required) 60acc48c Email (required) b5ea76a7 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: cc04005c First Name (required) 5cfcfc67 Last Name (required) 2bfdceab Email (required) 0fdfa56e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 05486c98 Last Name (required) f26032b3 Email (required) 3450b011 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These 