    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/department-chair-electrical-and-computer-engineering-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Department Chair - Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Department Chair - Electrical and Computer Engineering - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Department Chair - Electrical and Computer Engineering - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Department Chair - Electrical and Computer Engineering 45002488 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Faculty Administrator College Of Engineering MBU The Opportunity The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) in the Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) College of Engineering invites applications for the position of Department Chair, with an anticipated start in Fall 2027. The Chair will provide strategic leadership for a growing department with strong research momentum, expanding academic programs, and extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. About the Department Located within Virginia's premier urban research (R1) university, ECE enrolls approximately 350 students and offers bachelor's, master's, and doctoral programs, including a new master's program in systems engineering. The department includes 19 tenured, tenure-track, and term faculty. Faculty pursue research spanning micro- and nanoelectronics and photonics; optoelectronic and RF systems; semiconductor science; computer architecture and cyber-physical systems; artificial intelligence and edge technologies; robotics and autonomous systems; signal processing; communications and networking; smart and connected systems; and power, energy, and controls. They collaborate broadly across VCU, including with the university's medical campus, and with industry and government partners. ECE also plays a significant role in the College's multidisciplinary Robotics and Autonomous Systems program, collaborating with Computer Science and Mechanical and Nuclear Engineering. The department is committed to maintaining state-of-the-art facilities and instrumentation that support its research and educational missions. Learn more: https://egr.vcu.edu/departments/electrical-computer-engineering/ About the VCU College of Engineering Established in 1996 through a public-private partnership, the VCU College of Engineering is undergoing significant growth and transformation under new leadership. The College is expanding its faculty, interdisciplinary research, and educational offerings while advancing high-impact work in pharmaceutical engineering; smart cities, sustainability, and nuclear energy; advanced materials; health care, regenerative medicine, rehabilitation, and medical devices; data science; and cybersecurity and cyber-physical systems. Its entrepreneurial approach immerses undergraduate and graduate students in meaningful research throughout their studies. The College's graduate and online master's programs are nationally ranked and attract students from across the United States and around the world. Signature initiatives include the Medicines for All Institute, an international leader in reducing pharmaceutical costs for underserved populations; the Convergence Lab, a Department of Defense-funded cross-disciplinary institute addressing national defense challenges; and leadership of the Central Virginia Node of the Commonwealth Cyber Initiative, a state-supported engine for cybersecurity research, innovation, and commercialization. About VCU and Richmond VCU is a Carnegie-classified university with very high research activity and ranks among the top 100 U.S. universities and the top 50 public universities in federal research and development expenditures. The university's location in Richmond, Virginia's vibrant, art-filled, and culturally rich capital, creates exceptional opportunities for engagement with government, health care, industry, and the community. Washington, D.C., and major federal research agencies, including NSF, NIH, DOD, DOE, and DARPA, are approximately two hours away. Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in computer engineering, electrical engineering, or a closely related field. An internationally recognized record of scholarship, research, and academic achievement commensurate with appointment as a tenured professor. Demonstrated management and leadership accomplishments through progressively responsible faculty and administrative roles. A well-developed scholarly and research portfolio, including interdisciplinary applications and success in securing external funding, that complements and expands the department's strengths. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a staff member at VCU. Key Responsibilities Teaching Maintains an active faculty role through teaching and/or supervision of undergraduate and graduate students, consistent with departmental needs, institutional expectations, and the Chair's administrative responsibilities. Supports excellence in teaching and learning within the department, promotes innovative and effective instructional practices, and works with faculty to ensure appropriate curriculum development, assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement. Research and Scholarly Activity Maintains an active program of scholarly and/or professional activity appropriate to the discipline and institutional mission. Supports and advances the department's research, innovation, and scholarly priorities; promotes interdisciplinary and collaborative research; facilitates external funding opportunities; and supports faculty and student engagement in research and other scholarly activities. Service Provides service to the department, college/school, university, profession, and broader community as appropriate. Represents the department with internal and external stakeholders and develops partnerships with industry, government, professional organizations, alumni, and other constituencies. Promotes the visibility, reputation, and advancement of the department and its programs. Administration and Leadership Provides strategic and operational leadership for the department, including academic planning; faculty and staff recruitment and development; human resources matters; budgeting and resource allocation; enrollment and program planning; assessment, accreditation, and compliance. Leads the development and implementation of departmental goals and priorities in alignment with college and university strategic plans. The Chair oversees departmental operations and fosters a collaborative, open, and collegial environment that supports faculty, staff, and student success. The Chair works closely with faculty and college leadership on curriculum development, program quality, enrollment management, research development, student recruitment and retention, and long-term departmental planning. The Chair also advocates for departmental resources and represents the department in institutional and external forums. How to Apply Applicants should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, and the names and email addresses of four references. Reference letters will be requested for finalists. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For additional information, contact Arvind Agarwal, Ph.D. , Chair of the Search Committee, at agarwala15@vcu.edu . Unit: College Of Engineering Department: Electrical and Computer Engineering Salary Range: C ommensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Flexible Work Arrangement: Hybrid ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Professor Tenure: Tenure Track/Tenured Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Dr. Arvind Agarwal Contact Email: agarwala15@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 37914fba Last Name (required) fd23373e Email (required) a95de64c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 5f1ece3e First Name (required) 83ef07b1 Last Name (required) 7d376a50 Email (required) 916c6c25 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) d9db0c2c Last Name (required) ea57cf40 Email (required) 211f19cf Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance.