    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/transfusion-medicine-assistant-associate-professor-pathology-som-m89948-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Transfusion Medicine Assistant/Associate Professor | Pathology | SOM-M89948",
      "description": "Transfusion Medicine Assistant/Associate Professor | Pathology | SOM-M89948 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Transfusion Medicine Assistant/Associate Professor | Pathology | SOM-M89948 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Transfusion Medicine Assistant/Associate Professor | Pathology | SOM-M89948 45002423 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Pathology Department Summary: The Department of Pathology at Virginia Commonwealth University School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Assistant or Associate Professor (commensurate with experience) with expertise in clinical pathology and transfusion medicine. Duties & Responsibilities: Clinical: Serve as Transfusion Medicine/Apheresis attending. Medical direction of blood bank related clinical services, as needed. Provide medical oversight to all medical, technical and regulatory processes and procedures, including quality assurance. Promote the use of safe and effective blood transfusion components and services throughout the medical center, working closely with clinicians in hematology, oncology, stem cell transplantation, neurology, obstetrics and cardiothoracic and trauma surgery. Service: Participation in departmental, institutional and national committees when necessary. Teaching: Participation in the educational activities of Transfusion Medicine including: (1) didactic presentations, rounds, and seminars involving residents, medical and graduate students, and dental and allied health students; (2) continuing education for faculty, nurses, allied health personnel, and community physicians; and (3) development of workshops at the local, state, and national level. Research: Scholarship primarily in Pathology through presentations at national meetings, developing clinical research collaborations, contributions to peer-reviewed scientific literature, active participation in appropriate professional organizations is required. The faculty member will report to and work closely with the Division Chair to further the mission and vision of the Department of Pathology. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications MD, MD/PhD, or equivalent degree Board certification by the American Board of Pathology in combined Anatomic and Clinical Pathology or Clinical Pathology, or board certification in adult or pediatric Hematology/Oncology Board certification or eligibility in Transfusion Medicine Strong interest in and/or documented experience in laboratory management A scholarly record of publication in books and peer-reviewed journals Full, unrestricted medical licensure in Virginia Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Restricted: No Contact Email: SOMHR@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) e8c6daa1 Last Name (required) c4b70a95 Email (required) f6c27891 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Jo