    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/adjunct-field-liaison-school-of-social-work-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states-b0c16b64-a9d8-4595-84e8-926a106875e3": {
      "title": "Adjunct Field Liaison- School of Social Work",
      "description": "Adjunct Field Liaison- School of Social Work - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Adjunct Field Liaison- School of Social Work - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Adjunct Field Liaison- School of Social Work 45002467 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Academic and Faculty Affairs Faculty Adjunct School Of Social Work MBU The VCU School of Social Work, Office of Field Education, is hiring field education liaisons to oversee the field education of social work students completing the MSW Program. Field Liaisons serve as a link between the School of Social Work, field instructor and student. The roles and responsibilities of the field liaison include: ● Orienting students to the field course ● Providing students with a syllabus outlining expectations for the field course ● Facilitating monthly virtual class sessions ● Reading and grading student field course work requirements in a timely manner ● Assigning final field education grades based on all gathered course data, including but not limited to field instructor’s evaluation, assessment of field course work, and information derived from liaison conferences ● Providing feedback to students regarding their progress in field education providing consultation and support to students when there are difficulties in field education ● Helping field instructors design meaningful field education experiences for students ● Making virtual agency visits via video conferencing and maintaining ongoing contact with the field instructor and student ● Being available to students and field instructors for consultation and problem solving ● Adhering to the Office of Field Education’s policies and practices to support student success in field education ● Attending and actively participating in monthly virtual field liaison meetings ● Working directly with the Office of Field Education when student or agency related issues arise ● Participate in all field liaison trainings and orientations ● Providing ongoing evaluation of the placement agency and field instructor’s willingness and ability to provide learning opportunities and field instruction consistent with the learning objectives of the M.S.W. curriculum as set forth by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) ● Informing the student’s adviser when the student is experiencing difficulty in field education or is at risk of failing field education ● Other duties as assigned This is a part-time, non-benefited appointment Salary: $4,626 (full caseload, up to 17 students) $2,313 (half caseload, up to 11 students) Your application will become part of the Talent pool, which will be accessed only when an opening arises. If a suitable opening becomes available, we will review your qualifications. Please be aware that we are unable to hire applicants who are not already in the Talent pool. This position does not provide a formal pathway to full-time employment with Virginia Commonwealth University. Required Qualifications: ● MSW Degree from a CSWE accredited social work program ● Minimum of three years post MSW practice experience ● Previous field education experience as a field instructor or other social work education related experience ● Flexibility in schedule during the traditional work day ● Demonstrated experience working in and fostering an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from various backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications: ● Served as field instructor for a minimum of two years ● Five years of post MSW practice experience ● Previous higher education teaching experience with a focus on social work education or a related field ● Knowledge of non-profit and government social service agencies in the state of Virginia Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) ce58c37c Last Name (required) c1afd441 Email (required) 8b9830eb Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: e03b8bd4 First Name (required) 8c0d12f7 Last Name (required) 4ae977f0 Email (required) fcf9ab68 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator.