    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/assistant-professor-bachelor-of-science-in-health-services-program-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Bachelor of Science in Health Services Program",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Bachelor of Science in Health Services Program - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor - Bachelor of Science in Health Services Program - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor - Bachelor of Science in Health Services Program 45002412 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty College of Health Professions MBU Advertising Summary: The Bachelor of Science in Health Services Program, housed in the College of Health Professions, is seeking a student-focused Assistant Professor to coordinate the student internship experience in partnership with the Assistant Program Director. Additionally, the Assistant Professor will have teaching, research, and service expectations. Unit: College of Health Professions MBU Department: Deans Office AHP Department Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University seeks to create a work environment and organizational culture that reflects the variety of communities in which it is located and a climate for the success of every employee by appreciating the uniqueness that each one brings to the workplace. Our goal is to provide an environment where learners are successful in finding opportunities in the health care workspace. Overall program excellence is achieved by providing learners with a varied, context-responsive, and adaptive curriculum delivered by an interdisciplinary faculty, who aim to provide learners with the broad range of perspectives, insights, and knowledge they will need to succeed professionally. Excellence in the Bachelor of Science in Health Services program is a direct reflection of the professional, personal, and community-focused aspirations of our learners. The Bachelor of Science in Health Services program serves VCU undergraduate students seeking opportunities in healthcare. The mission is to provide an innovative pathway for students to explore their strengths and align them with a healthcare profession. The interdisciplinary program focuses on mentoring students, identifying their strengths and providing them with a safe environment to explore and grow. We also offer multiple minors that are available to all undergraduate VCU students that are interested in expanding their understanding of health care. Duties & Responsibilities: Internship Management The primary responsibility of this faculty member will be to work with the Assistant Program Director to build and implement high-quality internship experiences in alignment with the new vision of VCU Academic Affairs. This role will involve developing and maintaining partnerships with organizations across Virginia, expanding opportunities for students in various geographic and professional settings. The faculty member will also support both in-person and remote students throughout their internship experiences, ensuring meaningful engagement, mentorship, and professional development opportunities. Be a key member in the development of the mentorship program and support our career development course. Support students in finding internship placements and providing oversight of students throughout the semester which is done through our internship course which is offered to students in the Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. The coordinator will be responsible for initiating and maintaining relationships with potential internship sites (health centers, community-based organizations) for both the HSV major and two minors (research ecosystem and dental administration). The coordinator will also work with organizations the student identifies as potential internship sites. The coordinator will work to ensure that all policies, procedures and documentation of internship sites are consistent with VCU Academic Affairs' vision for internships. Teaching The faculty member will have asynchronous and face-to-face teaching responsibilities in ALHP 435 Health Care Career Development and Planning in Allied Health Professions and a minimum of two other core courses within Bachelor of Science in Health Services curriculum: Health Services, Bachelor of Science (B.S.) Virginia Commonwealth University Academic Catalog The faculty member will instruct courses in both the face-to-face program and asynchronous online program. The faculty member will provide support for students in their courses through providing regular student hours and timely, high quality assignment feedback. The faculty member will work with the Bachelor of Science in Health Services program in the development of new general education and restricted electives as needed. Service The faculty member will serve on their home departmental, College, and/or University committees as necessary, as well as in a professional capacity in their field (e.g., reviewer, conference organizer, etc.). The faculty member will play an active role in instructor course pods, helping to lead the continued improvement of program courses. Research While this position’s primary purpose is instruction, there may also be opportunities to engage in collaborative research and scholarship. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications PhD or terminal degree in a health-related or educational field. Minimum of two years managing or working in an internship type program with undergraduate students in health-related positions. Demonstrated teaching experience in a minimum of two of the linked teaching areas in an asynchronous online/hybrid/in-person environment. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching courses across multiple modalities (in-person, synchronous online, hybrid, hy-flex, etc). Experience leading student organizations, workshops, or student meetings online. Minimum of one year teaching in a LMS platform. Salary Range: $90,000+ (commensurate with experience) Benefits : All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Hybrid Rank: Assistant Professor Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Dr. Waggy Zeleke Contact Email: zelekew@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 9da0f642 Last Name (required) 5120d4cd Email (required) c57ff068 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 00a3af6e First Name (required) 753a90df Last Name (required) 7f1d662d Email (required) af90122e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of