    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/adjunct-instructor-introduction-to-contemporary-digital-culture-vcuarts-qatar-qatar": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor – Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture - VCUarts Qatar - Qatar",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor – Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture - VCUarts Qatar - Qatar Adjunct Instructor – Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture - VCUarts Qatar - Qatar Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Adjunct Instructor – Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture - VCUarts Qatar 45002439 Qatar Faculty Adjunct Qatar Campus MBU VCUarts Qatar invites applications for an adjunct faculty position under Academic Affairs to teach Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture , an undergraduate minor course exploring digital systems, platform culture, and the social, ethical, and cultural implications of digital dependency. The course investigates how digital systems have become embedded in everyday life and how platforms, algorithms, interfaces, data collection, and digital technologies shape human behavior, communication, relationships, identity, and culture. Rather than treating digital tools as neutral or optional, Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture asks students to critically examine the structures and power dynamics that influence digitally mediated environments. Special attention is given to how digital dependency is experienced across different cultural, regional, and social contexts, including contexts where digital access, autonomy, and digital safety create distinct challenges and opportunities. Course Focus The selected adjunct instructor will guide students through critical analysis, ethnographic observation, and design-based inquiry. Students will examine their own and others’ digital practices, develop awareness of patterns of digital dependency and engagement, and explore the ethical, social, and psychological implications of contemporary digital life. By the end of the course, students should be able to: Develop critical awareness of how digital systems and platforms structure contemporary life and shape human behavior. Analyze digital practices through ethnographic observation and identify patterns of dependency and engagement. Examine the power structures, algorithms, and data flows that underlie digital systems. Understand how digital dependency and digital awareness are experienced differently across cultures, geographies, and communities. Articulate the ethical, social, and psychological implications of living in digitally mediated environments. Key Responsibilities Teach Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture in accordance with the approved course description, learning outcomes, and expectations of Academic Affairs. Develop and deliver course materials, readings, assignments, discussions, critiques, and assessments that support student learning. Facilitate critical reflection, ethnographic observation, and design-based inquiry related to digital systems, platform culture, and digitally mediated environments. Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. Maintain regular communication with students and Academic Affairs regarding course expectations, progress, and academic matters. Foster a respectful, civil, and intellectually engaging classroom environment. Comply with university policies, academic procedures, and applicable guidelines. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in a relevant discipline or closely related field, such as media studies, communication, digital culture, design studies, anthropology, sociology, science and technology studies, art/design history, or another related field. Demonstrated teaching experience at the university level or relevant professional experience in a field related to digital culture, media, technology, design, or critical studies. Strong written and verbal communication skills in English. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCUarts Qatar. Eligibility to work in Qatar or meet applicable immigration/employment requirements under Qatari law. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree, such as a PhD, MFA, or equivalent, in a relevant field. Experience teaching interdisciplinary courses, minors courses, general education, media studies, digital culture, design studies, or related subjects. Familiarity with ethnographic methods, design-based inquiry, critical theory, platform studies, algorithmic culture, digital ethics, or digital safety. Experience teaching in international or multicultural higher education environments. Evidence of innovative, student-centered, and discussion-based teaching practices. Application Materials Applicants must submit the following through the VCU Jobs website: A current CV. A letter of interest outlining relevant teaching experience, professional background, and approach to teaching Introduction to Contemporary Digital Culture . List of three current references including names, phone numbers, and email addresses (references will not be contacted prior to applicant’s approval). Only applications submitted through the VCU Jobs website will be considered. Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 29285204 Last Name (required) c5879ee2 Email (required) a5dc2807 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 547d76f7 First Name (required) b0facbfa Last Name (required) 2d49547d Email (required) 0eecd2ed Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) b9bc3de1 Last Name (required) ccdac1ce Email (required) be7a1315 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along with third party non-persistent and persistent cookies to collect non-identifiable data from site visitors. VCU uses this collected data to prioritize and improve the content it delivers to its site visitors and to promote the university in a manner that is most relevant to its site visitors. I do not accept I accept"
