    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/senior-research-faculty-college-of-health-professions-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Research Faculty - College of Health Professions",
      "description": "Senior Research Faculty - College of Health Professions - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Senior Research Faculty - College of Health Professions - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Senior Research Faculty - College of Health Professions 45002395 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Research Teaching & Research Faculty College of Health Professions MBU Advertising Summary: The VCU College of Health Professions invites applications for a senior tenure-track faculty position specializing in Brain Health and Neurodegeneration. We seek an established, highly motivated, visionary scientist with a consistent record of extramural funding, interdisciplinary collaboration, and leadership in advancing knowledge of brain health and neurodegenerative disorders - including research examining topics from cell-to-society and biological, behavioral, and/or social factors influencing optimal outcomes. Institutional Investment & Growth Trajectory This position is part of a University-wide initiative to recruit high-impact tenured faculty members to support its rapidly growing, transformative research portfolio, with University sponsored research awards of more than $550m in FY25. The College of Health Professions is collaborating with the Office of the Provost and the Office of the Vice President for Research and Innovation to identify talented research faculty. Strategic Alignment & Scope This hire aligns with the CHP strategic priority to build on current expertise in brain health, aging, and neurodegenerative conditions across the lifespan and will amplify scientific discovery and dissemination in Neurodegeneration and Aging. The candidate will catalyze an interdisciplinary, cohesive, and comprehensive research agenda, leveraging VCU’s status as a top-tier research university to advance health equity, improve health outcomes, and optimize health care delivery. This strategic priority position provides a competitive salary and a generous start-up package. The College of Health Professions also offers a dedicated pre- and post-award research management team to ensure seamless grant transfers and/or grant administration. Unit: College of Health Professions Department: Deans Office AHP Department Summary: An Unmatched Interdisciplinary Ecosystem The College of Health Professions’ research vision is to discover research innovations that impact health outcomes and health care delivery. As a highly interdisciplinary college located in a vibrant academic medical campus, our research faculty share expertise in and passion for the intersection of neurodegenerative conditions, brain health, and healthy aging across multiple domains and perspectives. The College includes 9 departments with professions spanning the continuum of care, from bench (medical laboratory sciences) to bedside (e.g., occupational and physical therapy) to health and community systems (e.g., health administration, gerontology), and is home to the Virginia Center on Aging. We are uniquely positioned within a thriving health sciences campus and share this passion for neuroscientific research and neurodegenerative disorders with colleagues in, for example, the Schools of Public Health, Nursing, Pharmacy, and Medicine. The environment fosters interdisciplinary collaboration to meet our collective university-wide mission of excellence in research, teaching, and service that fosters innovations in practice and translational science, thus improving the quality of human life, solving complex challenges, and restoring health for all people. For more information about the position, the College of Health Professions, and Richmond, VA, please click here: https://chp.vcu.edu/about/careers/brain-health/ Duties & Responsibilities: Research & Scholarship Program of Research: Develop and lead an internationally recognized research program in neurodegeneration, brain health, and health sciences. Grant Acquisition: Secure competitive external funding from national and international agencies to support research activities, with a focus on R-level, Center, and training grants. Dissemination: Publish high-impact peer-reviewed articles and disseminate findings to academic, clinical, and public audiences. Collaboration: Build interdisciplinary collaborations across VCU, health professions, neuroscience, rehabilitation sciences, and public health. Teaching & Mentorship Teach and mentor faculty, postdoctoral fellows, and students in areas such as neurobehavioral science, brain health, research methods, grant writing, and similar. Contribute to graduate and professional education in health professions and neurobehavioral science. Service & Leadership Provide leadership in departmental, college, and university committees. Participate in strategic initiatives related to research infrastructure and capacity. Engage with the Richmond and surrounding communities, healthcare providers, patient advocacy groups, and community organizations to ensure research is relevant and translates to community needs, aligning with VCU’s mission as a community-engaged institution. Contribute to policy discussions, review panels, editorial boards, and evidence-based guidelines for neurodegenerative care to accelerate the translation of science into practice. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Education: PhD or equivalent terminal research degree in Health Professions, Neuroscience, Rehabilitation Sciences, Psychology, or a related field Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor (tenure-eligible) Sustained record of scholarly productivity, recent extramural funding (R01 or similar) as Principal Investigator, and currently funded with a history of success in securing major research grants and managing large-scale projects Demonstrated expertise in the study of neurodegenerative diseases (e.g., Alzheimer’s, Parkinson’s, ALS) across the continuum of care Commitment to research that complements and amplifies existing expertise in the College of Health Professions and VCU Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Eligible for licensure in Virginia as applicable Experience mentoring doctoral students, post-doctoral trainees, and new faculty Experience with biomarkers, surveillance, prevention, intervention, or implementation science Commitment to interdisciplinary and translational research Vision for advancing health professions and health sciences in prevention and care in neurodegenerative conditions Salary Range: $200,000 - $275,000 + Start Up Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Hybrid Rank: Open Tenure: Tenure Track Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Drs. Faika Zanjani & Lana Sargent Contact Email: fzanjani@vcu.edu & lsargent@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 8fa6235f Last Name (required) b39a467a Email (required) 6225f411 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 59baafdd First Name (required) 1c0ecad8 Last Name (required) 4f8fd5f2 Email (required) a8515f56 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 92294151 Last Name (required) 743756ed Email (required) 40b49755 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along