    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/senior-researcher-in-mental-health-and-brain-health-school-of-nursing-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Researcher in Mental Health and Brain Health, School of Nursing",
      "description": "Senior Researcher in Mental Health and Brain Health, School of Nursing - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Senior Researcher in Mental Health and Brain Health, School of Nursing - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Senior Researcher in Mental Health and Brain Health, School of Nursing 45002399 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Nursing MBU Unit: School of Nursing Department: Adult Health and Nursing Systems Mission or Goal of Unit: We champion health and well-being through the power of nursing education, discovery and practice. Chief Purpose of this position: The VCU School of Nursing invites applications for a senior tenure-track faculty position to lead a high-impact research program in Mental Health and/or Brain Health. We seek an established scientist with a consistent track record of extramural funding whose work is grounded in a life course perspective—examining how biological, behavioral, and social factors intersect at critical developmental stages to influence neurocognitive and mental health outcomes. Institutional Investment & Growth Trajectory This position is part of a University-wide initiative to recruit high-impact tenured faculty members to support its rapidly growing, transformative research portfolio, with University sponsored research awards of $550m+ in FY25. The School of Nursing is collaborating with the Office of the Provost and the Office of the Vice President for Research and Innovation to identify talented research faculty. Strategic Alignment & Scope This position is a strategic priority designed to bridge the SON’s existing strengths in maternal/perinatal health and aging/dementia and to amplify the impact of VCU’s existing interdisciplinary research in the field. The successful candidate will serve as a catalyst for interdisciplinary collaboration, leveraging VCU’s status as a top-tier public research university to advance health equity, improve health outcomes, and optimize health care delivery for vulnerable populations. This strategic priority position provides a competitive salary and a generous start-up package. An Unmatched Interdisciplinary Ecosystem The VCU School of Nursing is at the forefront of innovation and excellence. We are uniquely positioned within a thriving health sciences campus and share this passion for neuroscience and mental health research with colleagues in, for example, the Schools of Medicine, Public Health, Pharmacy, and College of Health Professions. This environment fosters rich, interdisciplinary collaboration to meet our collective university-wide mission of excellence in research, teaching, and service that fosters innovation in practice and translational science, thus improving the quality of human life, solving complex challenges, and restoring health for all people. Key Responsibilities 1. Research & Scholarship Program of Research: Maintain a robust, externally funded research portfolio focused on mental health, neuroscience/ brain health, and/or cognitive aging Grant Acquisition: Secure consistent extramural funding (e.g., NIH/NINR, AHRQ, PCORI, HRSA) to support research activities, with a focus on R-level, Center, and training grants Dissemination: Publish findings in high-impact, peer-reviewed journals and present at national/international policy and scientific forums Collaboration: Partner with interdisciplinary colleagues across VCU and beyond to address complex systems-level challenges 2. Teaching & Mentoring Teach and mentor students across programs and faculty/ trainees, providing relevant expertise in areas such as neuro/biobehavioral science, mental health, research methods, grant-writing, implementation science, and similar 3. Service & Leadership Provide leadership in departmental, college, and university committees Participate in strategic initiatives related to research infrastructure and capacity Contribute as thought-leaders to policy discussions, review panels, editorial boards and similar to accelerate the translation of science into practice Community Impact: Engage with the Richmond community and beyond to ensure research is relevant and translatable to community needs, aligning with VCU’s mission as a community-engaged institution Minimum Qualifications PhD or equivalent terminal degree in Nursing, Neuroscience, Psychology, Public Health, Medicine, or related field Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor (tenure-eligible) Distinguished record of scholarly productivity, recent extramural funding (R-level, Center grants, training grants, or equivalent) as Principal Investigator, and current funding with a history of success in securing major research grants and managing large-scale projects Demonstrated commitment to research that complements and amplifies existing expertise in the School of Nursing and VCU ( https://nursing.vcu.edu/research/faculty-research-and-scholarship-interests/) Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications If a registered nurse, eligibility for RN licensure in Virginia and a minimum of 2 years of previous clinical experience Experience mentoring doctoral students and junior faculty/post-doctoral trainees Experience with biobehavioral measurement (e.g., biomarkers, imaging), prevention, intervention, translational, or implementation science in mental health and brain health areas Commitment to and track record of interdisciplinary collaboration across health sciences schools Salary Range: Commensurate with experience FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Hybrid Rank: Open Tenure: Tenure Track Months: 12 months Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. Contact Information: Contact Name: Drs. Lana Sargent & Faika Zanjani Contact Email: lsargent@vcu.edu & fzanjani@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 7f4f6b09 Last Name (required) bbcf3166 Email (required) 3104c89f Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 0b7995df First Name (required) 460fc913 Last Name (required) d8d0b296 Email (required) 34851ebb Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 5c8dd932 Last Name (required) 4bb42c4a Email (required) 7e33fd5b Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to 