    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/center-for-team-care-med-peds-physician-department-of-internal-medicine-m89453-3-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Center for Team Care Med-Peds Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M89453 (3)",
      "description": "Center for Team Care Med-Peds Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M89453 (3) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Center for Team Care Med-Peds Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M89453 (3) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Center for Team Care Med-Peds Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M89453 (3) 45001280 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Department Summary: Mission or goal of unit: To deliver exceptional, affordable, and accessible care to VCU Health employees with an unwavering commitment to quality and experience. Chief Purpose of this position: The Center for Team Care (CTC) is a workforce wellness initiative within the VCU Health system to deliver high value, comprehensive, and concierge like primary care to VCU Health employees and dependents. The CTC is seeking experienced primary care physicians who can deliver high quality, high value care with a focus on population management and uncompromising patient experience. The ideal candidate will have experience working in a busy primary care practice with a focus on value based or concierge care. The ideal candidate will have experience delivering care in a holistic and lifestyle grounded approach. Duties & Responsibilities: Clinical | Serve as a primary care physician to a complex panel of patients, delivering high quality acute and episodic care, chronic disease management, and wellness care. Candidate will also be part of an interdisciplinary team to manage the preventive needs of a population of patients in addition to complying with billing, documentation, credentialing, and other administrative requirements. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board certification in Internal Medicine and/or Pediatrics At least 3-5 years of post-residency experience managing a complex patient panel in a busy primary care clinic. Eligible for Virginia Medical Licensure Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Experience in value-based care or concierge care Excellent vernal and written communication skills Experience working on an interdisciplinary team to manage a patient population Experience working or supervising APPs Experience or interest in working with pediatrics Experience in lifestyle medicine Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Samantha Flatley Contact Email: Samantha.Flatley@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 9ce9bd4c Last Name (required) a93b4752 Email (required) 38436043 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving y