      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Urban and Regional Studies and Planning Program (URSP)",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Urban and Regional Studies and Planning Program (URSP) - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Adjunct Instructor, Urban and Regional Studies and Planning Program (URSP) - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Adjunct Instructor, Urban and Regional Studies and Planning Program (URSP) 45000823 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Adjunct L D Wilder Sch of Govt & Pub Affrs Unit: L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs Department : Urban and Regional Studies and Planning Program The Urban and Regional Studies and Planning program in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs Program is recruiting a pool of applicants for possible adjunct teaching positions. The pool will be accessed as openings arise and the Program will contact persons in the pool whose credentials match our teaching needs. Duties: Teaching courses as needed. Ability to successfully teach both in-person and online. Must grade all assignments and exams in a timely manner. Ability to consistently respond to student inquiries within 24 hours. Ability to submit final grades according to school and university policy. Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s degree in Urban and Regional Planning or related field. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Urban and Regional Planning. Salary Range: $1,487 per credit ($4,461 for a 3-credit course). Rank: Instructor Tenure: Ineligible FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Application Instructions: All applications should include a cover letter, and detailed resume or curriculum vitae, with the names and contact information of three professional references. Contact Name: Meghan Gough, URSP Interim Program Chair Contact Email: mzgough@vcu.edu As a preeminent national, urban, public research university and academic health center, Virginia Commonwealth University is committed to an environment where all can thrive in their pursuit of excellence. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) cee0ed7c Last Name (required) 49432109 Email (required) 4c71404c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: cf42af72 First Name (required) c59b8079 Last Name (required) 52f588a4 Email (required) cf9bee0e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical cente