      "title": "Director of Radiopharmacy Assistant/Associate/Professor of Nuclear Pharmacy - VCU School of Pharmacy",
      "description": "Director of Radiopharmacy Assistant/Associate/Professor of Nuclear Pharmacy - VCU School of Pharmacy - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Director of Radiopharmacy Assistant/Associate/Professor of Nuclear Pharmacy - VCU School of Pharmacy - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director of Radiopharmacy Assistant/Associate/Professor of Nuclear Pharmacy - VCU School of Pharmacy 45002253 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Pharmacy MBU Advertising Summary: VCU School of Pharmacy's Department of Pharmacotherapy and Outcomes Science invites you to apply to the position of Assistant/Associate/Professor (non-tenure) of Nuclear Pharmacy as the Director of Radiopharmacy in the Stravitz-Sanyal Institute for Liver Disease and Metabolic Health (SSI). The faculty member shall be responsible for the development, production, and application of radiopharmaceuticals to support clinical and translational research initiatives at SSI. Duties include the formulation, quality assurance, and documentation of radioactive compounds for research protocols, as well as release of radiopharmaceuticals prior to injection. The faculty member will collaborate with investigators and imaging scientists to facilitate studies in molecular imaging, drug development, and disease characterization. Unit: School of Pharmacy Department: Pharmacotherapy and Outcomes Science About VCU VCU is a top 50 public research university with a genuine commitment to student success and community service. One of just a handful of universities to receive both a \"Very High Research Activity\" status and a \"Community Engaged\" designation from the Carnegie Foundation, VCU also hosts the region's top-rated medical center. The medical campus is home to top-ranked programs in Pharmacy, Medicine, Nursing, Dentistry, Public Health, and Health Professions, as well as the Center for Interprofessional Education and Collaborative Care, the Wright Center for Clinical and Translational Research, the Massey Comprehensive Cancer Center, the Pauley Heart Center, the Stravitz-Sanyal Institute for Liver Disease and Metabolic Health, among many other institutes and centers. About School of Pharmacy The School of Pharmacy (SOP) has a 127-year tradition beginning with the Medical College of Virginia and continuing to the present. Ranked in the Top 20 of Schools of Pharmacy nationwide, the SOP is dedicated to graduating outstanding future scientists and pharmacists who will develop new medicines and therapies, improve human health, foster exemplary research, and provide sustaining contributions to interprofessional patient care. As a full-time employee at VCU, you'll have access to a generous benefits package that includes health, vision, and dental coverage, life insurance, short- and long-term disability coverage, retirement plans, flexible spending accounts, tuition benefits, significant paid time off, and more. Explore our benefits here. About the Department of Pharmacotherapy & Outcomes Science The Department of Pharmacotherapy & Outcomes Science is one of three academic departments within the SOP and is a nationally recognized leader in pharmacy practice and education, personalized medicine, and health economics and outcomes research. Our faculty integrates expertise in pharmacotherapy, pharmacogenomics, digital health, social and administrative pharmacy, and pharmacoeconomics to advance medication optimization and population health. Faculty lead and collaborate through the Center for Pharmacy Practice Innovation (CPPI) to advance pharmacist-delivered care models and health policy initiatives, the Congressional Healthcare Policy Fellow Program to prepare pharmacists for public service, the Community-Based Pharmacy Residency Program to foster practice transformation across community settings, and the Geriatric Pharmacotherapy Program to enhance the delivery of healthcare to older adults. About Stravitz-Sanyal Institute for Liver Disease and Metabolic Health (SSI) The Stravitz-Sanyal Institute (SSI) at VCU aims to be a global leader in liver and metabolic-related research and education. With a team composed of world-renowned Hepatologists, the Institute strives to expand its research programs in changing the landscape of liver disease through research and innovation. Its clinical research imaging facility focuses on the advancement and development of novel imaging biomarkers and PET tracers, imaging methods, and data analysis tools to support the translation of emerging therapeutics in the liver and metabolic disease space. It is supported by a cGMP radiochemistry laboratory that is able to produce 18F, 68Ga (on-site), 64Cu and 89Zr PET biomarkers and radiopharmaceuticals. Our team members will engage in translational molecular research imaging at our new facility, to include a state-of-the-art research PET/CT scanner and radiochemistry laboratory, with the opportunity to engage with industry leaders and principal investigators. Chief Purpose of this position: ​ VCU School of Pharmacy's Department of Pharmacotherapy and Outcomes Science invites you to apply to the position of Assistant/Associate/Professor (non-tenure) of Nuclear Pharmacy as the Director of Radiopharmacy in the Stravitz-Sanyal Institute for Liver Disease and Metabolic Health (SSI). The faculty member shall be responsible for the development, production, and application of radiopharmaceuticals to support clinical and translational research initiatives at SSI. Duties include the formulation, quality assurance, and documentation of radioactive compounds for research protocols, as well as release of radiopharmaceuticals prior to injection . The faculty member will collaborate with investigators and imaging scientists to facilitate studies in molecular imaging, drug development, and disease characterization. Position Responsibilities: Research: Research responsibilities will be centered on the development, oversight, and advancement of radiopharmacy-related research within SSI, including the operation of the clinical research Imaging Center as it pertains to radiopharmacy areas. Significant effort is expected from the candidate to establish and sustain a nationally and internationally recognized research program in the areas described above by securing extramural funding and demonstrating an exceptional record of scholarship. Teaching: Significant effort is also expected to be devoted to teaching at the professional, graduate, and/or undergraduate levels in the School of Pharmacy. Service: The faculty member is expected to serve on departmental, School, and/or University committees as assigned, as well as in a professional capacity in their field, e.g., reviewer, conference organizer, etc. Other: Administrative duties. Minimum Qualifications: Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) degree and completed training to become an authorized nuclear pharmacist (ANP) Licensed or eligible for licensure in Virginia Board certified in Nuclear Pharmacy is required or must sit within 1 year of onboarding Must meet all requirements described in 10CFR35.55 to be listed as an Authorized Nuclear Pharmacist on VCU RAM license Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty member, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications: Leadership experience overseeing programs in the preparation and delivery of PET radiopharmaceuticals for use in research applications, as well study design/feasibility for studies that include radioactive substances Regulatory experience with regard to state and/or federal compliance on FDA-approved PET drugs, production, and use Experience with research protocols and clinical trials Regulatory experience with regard to state and/or federal submissions on RDRC or IND research studies and responding to FDA inquires related to CMC information Experience in developing and maintaining SOPs consistent with requirements set forth in 21CFR212, USP<823>, USP<825>, and USP<797>. Including components of aseptic manufacturing, environmental monitoring, vendor selection and qualification, material specification for ordering and associated review of relevant testing on receipt as part of quarantine procedures, continuous improvement, experience with QMS systems Experience as member of a Radioactive Drug Research Committee Experience in Radiochemistry development, quality control processes and cGMP compliance Experience in dose production and dispensing of novel radiotracers including long-lived and short-lived isotopes Experience with the receipt, storage, formulation, dispensing, and destruction of clinical test material and ensuring regulatory compliance within a compounding laboratory Experience in regulatory insight to GMP, USP, GCP requirements surrounding Phase I research Experience in formulating and compounding investigational drugs for use in Phase I studies with a focus on radiolabeled compounds Experience in writing research grants Preclinical research experience Salary Range: Commensurate with experience Benefits: All full-time university staff are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: Yes ORP Eligible: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Fully Onsite Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information Contact Name: Dr. Elvin T. Price Contact Email: etprice@vcu.edu The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit the following materials: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Summary of Research Interests and Plans Names and contact information for three references Please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Elvin T. Price (etprice@vcu.edu), for questions/clarifications regarding this position. Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) dfae5d38 Last Name (required) 0fd366ce Email (required) 500116d0 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 5a6037ca First Name (required) 0750a0f4 Last Name (required) 4cacc438 Email (required) b7f733f9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) bf89dc98 Last Name (required) b1138d31 Email (required) 089257b9 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along with third party non-persistent and persistent cookies to collect non-identifiable data from site visitors. VCU uses this collected data to prioritize and improve the content it delivers to its site visitors and to promote the university in a manner that is most relevant to its site visitors. I do not accept I accept"
