    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/primary-care-physician-family-medicine-with-obstetrics-fmob-community-memorial-hospital-family-medicine-som-m67726-south-hill-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Primary Care Physician – Family Medicine with Obstetrics (FMOB) | Community Memorial Hospital- Family Medicine | SOM | M67726",
      "description": "Primary Care Physician – Family Medicine with Obstetrics (FMOB) | Community Memorial Hospital- Family Medicine | SOM | M67726 - South Hill, Virginia, United States Primary Care Physician – Family Medicine with Obstetrics (FMOB) | Community Memorial Hospital- Family Medicine | SOM | M67726 - South Hill, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Primary Care Physician – Family Medicine with Obstetrics (FMOB) | Community Memorial Hospital- Family Medicine | SOM | M67726 45000978 South Hill, Virginia, United States Faculty Health Sciences MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Family Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: This position will be based at VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital in South Hill, Virginia. VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital is a small, rural community hospital that provides a wide range of subspecialty care to a large region. In 2017, VCU Health System built a beautiful, brand-new hospital that is both aesthetically and clinically spectacular. The family medicine residency clinic is attached to the hospital. Our department provides newborn nursery and inpatient pediatrics coverage. Current inpatient volumes are approximately 300 deliveries and 50 pediatrics admissions per calendar year. High acuity cases are transferred to a higher level of care. July 1, 2025, CMH welcomed its first class of family medicine residents. The residents spend their first year of training at our main campus in Richmond, approximately 75 miles to our north, and spend their second and third years in South Hill. Mission, History & Programs of the Department Founded in 1970, the Department of Family Medicine and Population Health at VCU has a long and proud history of training medical students and resident physicians. Our department houses our family medicine medical student education programs, including a highly rated clerkship and two longitudinal, four-year track programs. Our department is one of the top ten in the nation for family medicine research. We have four affiliated family medicine residency programs at various locations around the Commonwealth of Virginia in addition to our new VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital Family Medicine Residency, which will graduate its first class in 2027. Position Overview This position is a Family Medicine Obstetrics (FMOB) role, integrating outpatient primary care and comprehensive obstetrical services, with optional inpatient medicine and newborn care, within a rural training environment. The physician will serve as a residency faculty member in the Family Medicine Residency, supporting development of a robust FMOB training. Chief Purpose of the Position To practice broad scope rural family medicine and to train the next generation of family medicine physicians in Southside Virginia. This position includes clinical faculty appointment to the Department of Family Medicine and Population Health. Major Duties and Responsibilities Clinical Responsibilities (100%) Maintain a practice at the Family Medicine Residency Clinic through resident precepting and an optional outpatient panel (based on outpatient Family Medicine FTE). Provide full-spectrum FMOB care including prenatal, labor and delivery, postpartum, and newborn care. Participate in shared obstetrics call coverage. Optional participation in inpatient pediatric care and newborn nursery coverage. Optional participation in adult inpatient medicine. Teaching & Academic Responsibilities Precept residents and medical students in family medicine and obstetrics settings. Serve as faculty for FMOB curriculum development. Support development of rural FMOB training. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications MD/DO with eligibility for Virginia licensure. Completion of accredited Family Medicine residency. Board Certified/Eligible. Demonstrated competency in obstetrics including vaginal delivery. Experience in providing direct patient care to underserved populations across multiple settings Willing and able to care for patients in both the inpatient and outpatient settings. This position will include light newborn nursery and inpatient pediatrics call (facility currently has approx. 300 deliveries/year). Adult inpatient and pediatric/newborn services are optional for this position (facility currently has approximately 50 pediatric admissions/year). We incorporate proctoring as part of our onboarding process, so current inpatient privileges are not required. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications FMOB fellowship or equivalent experience. Experience with assisted delivery and/or cesarean section is strongly preferred. Rural practice and teaching experience. Experience in providing direct patient care and/or residency training in rural settings Direct experience in the medical education of learners such as residents, medical students, inter-professional learners Confidence and willingness to be a faculty lead in one or more of the following: Care of pregnant women including antenatal, labor and delivery including operative management, and postpartum care Care of adults in the inpatient setting Care of children in the inpatient setting Mental Health treatment in the primary care setting Substance abuse treatment to include medically assisted therapy Primary care Point of Care Ultrasound (POCUS) and/or specialized procedural training in emergency, inpatient and outpatient setting Leadership experience, preferably of a multi-site primary care group. Salary Range: Commensurate with experience FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No Rank: Open ORP Eligible: No Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Name: Ashley Krauss Contact Email: ashley.krauss@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 3ba4c70c Last Name (required) 38d32d23 Email (required) 85f62a64 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 22e5b46a First Name (required) 842a27bb Last Name (required) e8b2d4e8 Email (required) 109b6b0b Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 396decd4 Last Name (required) 68f927b7 Email (required) 5f83aed3 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages