      "description": "Gastroenterologist Physician (Community Memorial Hospital) | Department of Internal Medicine | M89487 - South Hill, Virginia, United States Gastroenterologist Physician (Community Memorial Hospital) | Department of Internal Medicine | M89487 - South Hill, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Gastroenterologist Physician (Community Memorial Hospital) | Department of Internal Medicine | M89487 45001408 South Hill, Virginia, United States Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Mission or goal of unit: The mission of the Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology is to strengthen the health of our rural community by providing accessible, high-quality digestive care, fostering strong partnerships with local providers, and supporting patients through every stage of diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management. Chief Purpose of this Position: The Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition at VCU is seeking a Board-Eligible/Board-Certified Gastroenterologist to join our team at Community Memorial Hospital, located in the scenic and welcoming community of South Hill, Virginia. J1 candidates are encouraged to apply. Ideal opportunity for a physician seeking a collaborative and supportive environment within a superb hospital system. Duties & Responsibilities: Clinical Monday - Friday 8 am - 5 pm schedule 10 days call coverage per month (evenings and weekends) Additional call pay available beyond 10 days 2 days clinic, 3 days procedures weekly Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board certified or board eligible in gastroenterology from an accredited training program Virginia licensure or ability to obtain Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty at VCU. Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Brooke Hayes Contact Email: Brooke.Hayes@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 7a5ed432 Last Name (required) 0c560f63 Email (required) 9c42a145 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 1c9ce104 First Name (required) 0e3ef08f Last Name (required) ec891fd0 Email (required) 4e78017c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU 