      "title": "PRN Pediatric Surgeon, Department of Surgery, (M89654)",
      "description": "PRN Pediatric Surgeon, Department of Surgery, (M89654) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States PRN Pediatric Surgeon, Department of Surgery, (M89654) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search PRN Pediatric Surgeon, Department of Surgery, (M89654) 45002199 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Surgery Duties & Responsibilities: The Department of Surgery, Division of Pediatric Surgery is recruiting for an open rank, collateral, non-tenure track PRN faculty position in the area of pediatric surgery. The faculty member will support the general surgical practice of the division. Finally, the faculty member will support the division with teaching responsibilities at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching : The faculty member will have teaching responsibilities in all areas of pediatric surgery. Research : This position will require the establishment of a successful research program in partnership with other disciplines which will lead to independent funding as an investigator. Other: The faculty member will serve on departmental, and/or university committees as necessary, as well as in a professional capacity in their field. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Must be board certified/board eligible in general surgery and pediatric surgery Completion of ACGME approved fellowship in pediatric surgery Ability to work in a complex matrixed environment with high emotional intelligence Commitment to teaching and practice in an academic setting Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Board eligibility or certification in pediatric critical care Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Contact Information: Contact Name: Mary Waite Contact Email: Mary.Waite@Vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 6cd14f46 Last Name (required) 4f5255ac Email (required) b41b52f8 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 21aa1f30 First Name (required) dd99efee Last Name (required) 62adb843 Email (required) d20c2620 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-o