      "description": "Gastroenterologist | Department of Intenral Medicine | M68131, M68132, M68133 (6) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Gastroenterologist | Department of Intenral Medicine | M68131, M68132, M68133 (6) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Gastroenterologist | Department of Intenral Medicine | M68131, M68132, M68133 (6) 45001652 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Mission or goal of unit: The mission of the Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology is to strengthen the health of our community by providing accessible, high-quality digestive care, fostering strong partnerships with local providers, and supporting patients through every stage of diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management. Chief Purpose of this Position: VCU Health is seeking a Board-Certified/Board-Eligible Luminal Gastroenterologists to join our expanding team at a new state-of-the-art outpatient pavilion located in Chesterfield County, VA. This premier facility will include an Ambulatory Surgery Center (ASC) and a Medical Office Building (MOB) designed to deliver patient-centered, comprehensive outpatient services to the Chesterfield community and surrounding regions. This facility will open in 2027. Duties & Responsibilities: 2 days clinic and 2 days procedures weekly with 1 administrative day at the Chesterfield County ambulatory surgical center (ASC) and Medical Office Building (MOB) 8-10 weeks of inpatient call at Downtown VCU Medical Center campus per year with fellows and residents Optional participation in case conferences with fellows Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board certified or board eligible in gastroenterology from an accredited training program Virginia licensure or ability to obtain General gastroenterology position Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty at VCU Preferred Qualifications Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Brooke Hayes Contact Email: Brooke.Hayes@vcuhelath.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 0a5b103a Last Name (required) 05f7c56b Email (required) 141832d0 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 3e00e1c2 First Name (required) ef7e2c00 Last Name (required) aac5b164 Email (required) 2dc94e78 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt