      "description": "Hand Surgeon PRN, Department of Surgery (M89629) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Hand Surgeon PRN, Department of Surgery (M89629) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Hand Surgeon PRN, Department of Surgery (M89629) 45001926 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Surgery MISSION OR GOAL OF UNIT: The mission of the Division of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery is to advance the science through research and the training. The Division provides faculty with specialized clinical and research environments to foster professional growth and provide exceptional care for the community, while maintaining a steadfast commitment to our staff and student body. CHIEF PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION IN SUPPORT OF ABOVE MISSION OR GOAL: This position is a PRN collateral, non-tenure track faculty position dedicated to assist with hand and upper extremity trauma call and subsequent care of patients from call. RESPONSIBILITIES 1. Teaching: Provide expert oversight for residents, fellows, and medical students in hand surgery while on call and in the operating room as needed. 2. Research: Support clinical or translational research projects focused on evidence-based outcomes in hand and wrist surgery. Mentoring students in investigating patient-centered recovery and innovative surgical techniques and support departmental quality improvement initiatives. 3. Service: Provide hand trauma call coverage as needed. 4. Clinical: Provide hand trauma call coverage as needed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery Commitment to Resident Education and teaching Commitment to Clinical Research and Innovation Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Candidate with fellowship experience in hand and microsurgery. Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Mary Waite Contact Email: Mary.Waite@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) b9dbf9a0 Last Name (required) bc241d59 Email (required) 6e23dfb8 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 44cc0d32 First Name (required) 17b9c2de Last Name (required) 644c7c00 Email (required) 4e21fbb9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth Uni