    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/general-surgeon-tappahannock-hospital-department-of-surgery-m68144-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "General Surgeon, Tappahannock Hospital, Department of Surgery (M68144)",
      "description": "General Surgeon, Tappahannock Hospital, Department of Surgery (M68144) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States General Surgeon, Tappahannock Hospital, Department of Surgery (M68144) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search General Surgeon, Tappahannock Hospital, Department of Surgery (M68144) 45001807 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Surgery Mission or Goal of Unit: The mission of the Department of Surgery is the pursuit of excellence in surgical care through constant innovation and education and to provide every patient with the best care. This position will reside in the Section of Community General Surgery under the Division of Bariatric and GI surgery. Chief Purpose of this position: This position is a junior to mid-level, term, non-tenure track faculty position. The incumbent will provide support at the General Surgery practice in the VCU Health Tappahannock Hospital, a 67 bed hospital in Tappahannock, Virginia. The faculty member will support the Section Community General Surgery at VCU Health Tappahannock Hospital with teaching responsibilities at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Position Responsibilities: Clinical The primary clinical responsibility will be in the care of the general surgery patients at VCU Health Tappahannock Hospital, and possibly in other VCUHS clinics and operative locations. They will be responsible for the development of an active general surgery practice, with the support of the Division and Department’s leadership. Teaching The faculty member will have teaching responsibilities as a part of their role. Oversight of trainees as well as instruction in General Surgery and applied anatomy and physiology. Research Faculty member may participate in research activities and/or collaborate with others on research projects and endeavors Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board Certification or Eligibility in General Surgery Commitment to teaching and education of medical students and other trainees Ability to work in a complex matrixed environment with a high emotional intelligence Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level. Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Mary Waite Contact Email: Mary.Waite@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 02e1c812 Last Name (required) 619a5cf3 Email (required) 82a6c091 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit