      "description": "Nephrologist | Department of Internal Medicine | M89542 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Nephrologist | Department of Internal Medicine | M89542 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Nephrologist | Department of Internal Medicine | M89542 45001510 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: Mission or goal of unit: Provide excellent, compassionate, evidence based, efficient patient care while educating the physicians and healthcare professionals of tomorrow using state-of-the-art facilities and knowledge. Chief Purpose of this Position : To contribute to and enhance the educational and clinical activities of the section of General Nephrology within the division of Nephrology by providing compassionate, efficient, high quality consultative patient care in outpatient and inpatient settings and support the research goals of the division and department. Teaching: Teach fellows, residents and medical students using adult teaching methods that enhance and encourage active learning and ongoing professional development. Complete student, resident and fellows evaluations. Participate in other Nephrology educational activities including resident didactic series, conferences, morning report, Nephrology and Internal Medicine Grand Rounds, and other educational duties assigned by the department and service. Research: Participate in clinical and administrative research according to skills, interest and funding. Provide mentoring and supervision of fellows and residents in research and QI initiatives. Research opportunities may include performance improvement initiatives or formal extramurally funded investigations and participation may be as principal investigator or co-investigator. Service: Work with institutional and administrative staff to attain the objectives of Virginia Commonwealth University and VCU Health System including patient safety, patient satisfaction, maintenance and enhancement of public perception and fiscal health. Clinical: Provide excellent patient care in Nephrology and focused areas of interest and experience in both inpatient and outpatient settings. Other (for instance administrative duties, etc.): Comply promptly with billing, documentation, credentialing and other administrative requirements of the department. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board certification or eligibility in Nephrology Direct experience in managing complex inpatients and outpatients Completion of accredited fellowship in General Nephrology Requires an interest in teaching and growth in an academic setting Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to work as a member of a team providing effective communication, both verbal and written and an interest in furthering the research, scholarly and academic missions of the division. Salary Range: Commensurate Benefits : All VCU employee types are eligible for a wide array of benefits to support you during your employment at VCU. Consult the benefits website for information on benefits eligibility according to employee type. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Rebecca Mullin Contact Email: Rebecca.Mullin@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) ac899337 Last Name (required) 712bb8e8 Email (required) 39da7960 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 88961997 First Name (required) c28023b3 Last Name (required) 6383a1ac Email (required) ffc4bf91 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety a