    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/orthopaedic-hand-and-soft-tissue-surgeon-orthopaedic-surgery-som-m68229-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Hand and Soft Tissue Surgeon | Orthopaedic Surgery | SOM | M68229",
      "description": "Orthopaedic Hand and Soft Tissue Surgeon | Orthopaedic Surgery | SOM | M68229 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Orthopaedic Hand and Soft Tissue Surgeon | Orthopaedic Surgery | SOM | M68229 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Orthopaedic Hand and Soft Tissue Surgeon | Orthopaedic Surgery | SOM | M68229 45001105 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Health Sciences MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Unit: School Of Medicine Department: Orthopedic Surgery Duties & Responsibilities: The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at VCU Health System is recruiting a board certified or eligible hand fellowship trained orthopaedic or plastic surgeon with an interest in hand and extremity (upper and lower) orthoplastic reconstruction and microvascular free tissue transfer. The candidate will provide diagnostic and interventional management for a full spectrum of hand and extremity reconstructive indications. The emphasis of the practice will be on reconstruction of traumatic and oncologic musculoskeletal injuries and both traumatic and atraumatic conditions of the hand. Completion of an ACGME accredited Hand Fellowship is desired but not required if applicant has adequate experience in complex hand trauma. The selected candidate will be expected to collaborate in investigative work that leads to publications in peer-reviewed journals and participate in both didactic and bedside teaching and mentoring activities for our medical students, residents, trauma and hand fellows. The position will be based at Virginia Commonwealth University Medical Center, a level 1, tertiary trauma center. Qualifications: A valid Virginia medical license MD or DO degree (or equivalent degree) from an accredited program Completed an ACGME accredited Orthopaedic or Plastic Surgery Residency program Board certification/eligibility in Orthopaedic Surgery or Plastic Surgery Applicants' materials must list current and/or pending qualifications upon submission. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Completion of an ACGME accredited Hand Fellowship is desired but not required if applicant has adequate experience in complex hand trauma. Salary Range: Commensurate with experience Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Name: Ashley Krauss Contact Email: ashley.krauss@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) dc57881b Last Name (required) 973390d5 Email (required) 919c01b3 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 10bdbf29 First Name (required) ff5d1324 Last Name (required) acb672b3 Email (required) 378b0dca Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Mai