    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/som-cardiothoracic-radiologist-m68190-m89556-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "SOM Cardiothoracic Radiologist (M68190 & M89556)",
      "description": "SOM Cardiothoracic Radiologist (M68190 & M89556) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States SOM Cardiothoracic Radiologist (M68190 & M89556) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search SOM Cardiothoracic Radiologist (M68190 & M89556) 45001597 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Health Sciences Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Radiology Duties & Responsibilities: Provide specialized cardiovascular imaging interpretation of conventional radiography, chest CT, HRCT, CTA, lung cancer screening, in addition to cardiac CTA and cardiovascular MR in an 865-bed VCU Medical Center with a six-bay Level 1 Trauma Center suite and referral center. Services are also provided by the Section for the Massey Cancer Center, Pauley Heart Center, Interstitial Lung Disease Institute, pre- and post-operative lung and heart transplantation care. This full-time cardiothoracic position will train medical students, residents and fellows within the large, highly productive academic radiology department. Position Responsibilities: Teaching – Provide training to medical students, residents and fellows, who rotate through the Department of Radiology. Clinical – Provide high quality, sub-specialized imaging interpretations for assigned modalities in support of the referring physicians and patients of VCUHS. Work collaboratively with a multidisciplinary team of pulmonologists, cardiologists, cardiothoracic surgeons, and other healthcare providers to provide accurate and timely diagnoses. Scholarly Activities - Faculty are encouraged to participate in activities related to national societies and organizations to maintain clinical excellence. Service – Time and effort is expected to be devoted to academic service-related activities. This shall include college, school, and departmental committee work, professional growth, and other such assignments. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications ABR certification or documentation of passing the Core Component of the ABR Board examination Be fellowship trained in Cardiothoracic Radiology and have an interest in teaching and research Candidates must be eligible for a Virginia medical license; must be eligible for permanent employment in the USA Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) b298ee0b Last Name (required) e5195a1b Email (required) 6ef71a4b Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 981a30e3 First Name (required) 6cfb2a0b Last Name (required) 113eeb4a Email (required) 984fd600 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for shar