      "description": "SOM Abdominal Imaging Radiologist (Radiology - M67573) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States SOM Abdominal Imaging Radiologist (Radiology - M67573) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search SOM Abdominal Imaging Radiologist (Radiology - M67573) 45001798 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU's sponsored research the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Radiology Duties & Responsibilities: To provide abdominal imaging interpretations, including abdominopelvic CT, MR, US, and GI/GU fluoroscopy procedures with the use of state-of-the-art equipment. Clinical- Provide high quality abdominal imaging interpretations for assigned modalities in support of the referring physicians and patients of VCUHS. Responsibilities include conventional radiographs, abdominopelvic CT, abdominopelvic MR, US and fluoroscopy procedures. Work closely with providers in primary care, gastroenterology, hepatology, oncology, nephrology, urology, surgical oncology, OB/ GYN, bariatric surgery, trauma, transplant, and general surgery, providing a high level of subspecialty expertise with the most advanced imaging options Teaching- Provide training to medical students, residents & fellows who rotate through the Department of Radiology Research- Continue to promote professional relationships and work closely with Surgery, Gastroenterology, Urology, Radiation Oncology and other departments/divisions to foster interdisciplinary research Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications ABR certification or documentation of passing the Core Component of the ABR Board examination Fellowship trained in Abdominal imaging Candidates must be eligible for a Virginia medical license Candidates be eligible for permanent employment in the USA Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Strong clinical background in imaging Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Laura Carucci, MD Contact Email: laura.carucci@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 0058e047 Last Name (required) 36582b97 Email (required) ae0655e1 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: be568bf4 First Name (required) e9d62ac9 Last Name (required) c1e82f12 Email (required) 0e502b91 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank yo