    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/hepatologist-department-of-internal-medicine-m68006-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Hepatologist | Department of Internal Medicine | M68006",
      "description": "Hepatologist | Department of Internal Medicine | M68006 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Hepatologist | Department of Internal Medicine | M68006 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Hepatologist | Department of Internal Medicine | M68006 45001059 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Department: Internal Medicine Mission or Goal of Unit: To provide superior, compassionate and innovative clinical care to our patients using state of the art knowledge and resources and to conduct and disseminate clinical research and scholarship, with a focus on the care of patients and education of future clinicians. Chief Purpose of this position: The Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition is seeking full-time Hepatologist, that is board eligible/certified in Gastroenterology and Hepatology to provide clinical services in the Hepatology clinics at VCU Health System, to include both clinics on the Medical College of Virginia Hospital campus and in Hepatology outreach locations. Duties & Responsibilities: Clinical - Provide clinical services in the hepatology clinics at VCUHS, to include both clinics on the MCVH campus and in outreach locations; participate in the inpatient management of patients with Liver conditions, perform diagnostic endoscopic procedures. Teaching - Provide teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows in the management of patients with Liver conditions. Research - The faculty will engage in research and develop interdisciplinary collaborations in support of the core mission. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible in Hepatology Experience in Hepatology research Eligible for Virginia Medical Licensure Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Brooke Hayes Contact Email: Brooke.Hayes@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 22a355de Last Name (required) 69126d4e Email (required) f2ba7893 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 8dfc3b9f First Name (required) 744665d0 Last Name (required) 6b619f16 Email (required) ebc533d3 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microb