    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/adult-congenital-heart-disease-physician-department-of-internal-medicine-m06547-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Adult Congenital Heart Disease Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M06547",
      "description": "Adult Congenital Heart Disease Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M06547 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Adult Congenital Heart Disease Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M06547 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Adult Congenital Heart Disease Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M06547 45001065 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Department: Internal Medicine Mission or Goal of Unit: At VCU Health Pauley Heart Center, our world-class team takes your heart health personally. Building on our history of innovation in patient care, scientific discovery and collaboration we improve cardiovascular care for all, while continuously training the next generation of providers. Chief Purpose of this position: The Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Cardiology is seeking a candidate to provide Adult Congenital Heart Disease clinical care along with supporting the academic mission in research and education. The ACHD program completed the accreditation site visit and institutionally has support for strong a program. The incumbent will join an established group of physicians and surgeons in one of the top Heart Centers in the United States. Duties & Responsibilities: The candidate will provide comprehensive care in the inpatient and outpatient setting for adults with congenital heart disease regardless of severity of illness. The candidate will collaborate with a multidisciplinary team of experts, including pediatric cardiologists, congenital and adult cardiac surgeons, interventional cardiologists, electrophysiologists, advanced heart failure and transplant specialists, hepatologists, social workers, nurses, and others. The candidate will participate in outreach clinics and in research and educational activities related to ACHD, such as publishing papers, presenting at conferences, teaching fellows and residents, and mentoring students. The candidate will assist in the development of an ACHD fellowship. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Must be a board certified cardiologist and board certified/board eligible in Adult Congenital Heart Disease Must be clinically oriented and possess sufficient research and teaching experience to be eligible for an academic appointment Must be able to communicate effectively and work with a large multi-disciplinary program Must participate in teaching and fellowship programs Eligible for medical licensure in the state of Virginia Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Michelle Carpenter Contact Email: Michelle.Carpenter@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 6788f4bf Last Name (required) 4bd1ff7a Email (required) ce5ce239 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 2aa730f3 First Name (required) 06f7ed5e Last Name (required) 5d1bbd7e Email (