    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/heart-failure-scholar-department-of-internal-medicine-division-of-cardiology-m67393-m67689-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Heart Failure Scholar | Department of Internal Medicine - Division of Cardiology | M67393 & M67689",
      "description": "Heart Failure Scholar | Department of Internal Medicine - Division of Cardiology | M67393 & M67689 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Heart Failure Scholar | Department of Internal Medicine - Division of Cardiology | M67393 & M67689 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Heart Failure Scholar | Department of Internal Medicine - Division of Cardiology | M67393 & M67689 45001381 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: Mission or goal of unit: At VCU Health Pauley Heart Center, our world-class team takes your heart health personally.Building on our history of innovation in patient care, scientific discovery and collaboration we improve cardiovascular care for all, while continuously training the next generation of doctors. Chief Purpose of this position: The Cardiology Heart failure scholars program is to allow for inpatient inhouse coverage on the Cardiology units at night 12 hours per day 7 days per week. The Cardiology Hospitalist service traditionally has been a 2 person team of internists who support the Cardiology inpatient teams in the care of patients with multiple medical problems and to support the expansion of CV services. The Heart Failure Scholars will be part of this rotation covering 1 week each in a 4 week rotation. In the remaining time, the scholar will rotate through efforts focused on clinical exposure to cardiology, heart failure, quality improvement and research. Teaching: To support teaching directly via interactions with Housestaff and non-physician professionals. Research: To support clinical research protocols in recruitment and adjunctive clinical management and to engage in scholarly activity. Learner: Participate in learning activity on inpatient consult services and ambulatory settings focused on exposure to clinical heart failure Clinical: Anticipated clinical effort is 25%. The workload and time commitments are commensurate with the medical hospitalists - nocturnists; duty hours will be 7 shifts per 4-week period of time. Duties: to directly manage patients on the inpatient and observational Cardiology services 12 hours overnight in a collaborative manner with the Cardiology faculty and Advanced Practice Providers (APPs). To provide Emergency Department consultations regarding Cardiology Admissions. To work collaboratively with Cardiology Attendings, Fellows, Residents and APPs to assure a unified Cardiology plan is developed for each patient. Other (for instance administrative duties, etc.): Submit billing and document care as required by the organization. Abide by all medical staff requirements. Participate in quality initiatives. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible in Internal Medicine Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Clinical and Scholarly interest in a Career in Heart Failure Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Con