    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/cardiology-hospitalist-department-of-internal-medicine-m60503-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Cardiology Hospitalist | Department of Internal Medicine | M60503",
      "description": "Cardiology Hospitalist | Department of Internal Medicine | M60503 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Cardiology Hospitalist | Department of Internal Medicine | M60503 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Cardiology Hospitalist | Department of Internal Medicine | M60503 45001608 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU This is an MCV Physicians job posting and opportunity. This is not a Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) job posting. None of the information or duties below is part of a job offered by VCU. Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Mission or Goal of Unit: At VCU Health Pauley Heart Center, our world-class team takes your heart health personally. Building on our history of innovation in patient care, scientific discovery, and collaboration we improve cardiovascular care for all, while continuously training the next generation of doctors. Chief Purpose of this Position : The cardiology hospitalist program provides for inpatient in-house coverage on the cardiology units at night 12 hours per day 7 days per week. The hospitalist service is a 2-person team of internists who support the cardiology inpatient teams in the care of patients with multiple medical problems and supports the expansion of CV services. This position is also responsible for coverage of chest pain level III patients in the emergency department. Duties & Responsibilities: Clinical: Anticipated clinical effort is 100%. The workload and time commitments are commensurate with the medical hospitalists - nocturnists; duty hours will be approximately 14 to 15 shifts per 4-week period of time. Faculty will directly manage patients on the inpatient and observational Cardiology services 12 hours overnight in a collaborative manner with the Cardiology faculty and Advanced Practice Providers (APPs). Will provide Emergency Department consultations regarding Cardiology Admissions and work collaboratively with Cardiology Attendings, Fellows, Residents and APPs to assure a unified Cardiology plan is developed for each patient. Teaching: To support teaching directly via interactions with Fellows, Housestaff and non-physician professionals. Research: To support clinical research protocols in recruitment and adjunctive clinical management. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible in Internal Medicine Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Advanced training in Critical Care Medicine Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Michelle Carpenter Contact Email: Michelle.Carpenter@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 8726a9f1 Last Name (required) 4f801a1a Email (required) f139d9fb Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 59258cc9 First Name (required) 78bfadf0 Last Name (required) ce861344 Email (required) 8cbf8b7f Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for