      "title": "Prevention and Cardiometabolic Disease (Non-Invasive Cardiologist) | Department of Internal Medicine | F65300",
      "description": "Prevention and Cardiometabolic Disease (Non-Invasive Cardiologist) | Department of Internal Medicine | F65300 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Prevention and Cardiometabolic Disease (Non-Invasive Cardiologist) | Department of Internal Medicine | F65300 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Prevention and Cardiometabolic Disease (Non-Invasive Cardiologist) | Department of Internal Medicine | F65300 45001068 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Unit: School of Medicine Department: Internal Medicine Mission or Goal of Unit: At VCU Health Pauley Heart Center, our world-class team takes your heart health personally. Building on our history of innovation in patient care, scientific discovery and collaboration we improve cardiovascular care for all, while continuously training the next generation of providers. Chief Purpose of this position: The Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Cardiology is seeking a board-certified or board-eligible Non-Invasive Cardiologist to provide clinical care. This position focuses on the prevention, early detection, and management of cardiovascular disease along with supporting our academic mission in research and education. Be part of a nationally recognized academic medical center while collaborating with a dynamic team of cardiologists, researchers, and educators. The incumbent will have access to state-of-the-art facilities and innovation in preventive cardiology. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching: Participate in teaching medical students, residents, and cardiology fellows. Research: To support clinical research protocols as needed. Service: Will be expected to participate in quality, safety and efficiency initiatives Clinical: Will primarily be dedicated to cardiovascular preventative services. Other (for instance administrative duties, etc.): Ensure timely and accurate documentation of clinical care and submission of billing in accordance with organizational policies. Comply fully with all medical staff bylaws, rules, and regulatory requirements. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications MD or DO degree with board certification or eligibility in cardiovascular disease Eligible for medical licensure in Virginia Clinically oriented and possess sufficient research and teaching experience to be eligible for academic appointment Must be able to communicate effectively and work with a large multidisciplinary program Must be willing to participate in teaching and fellowship programs Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Experience and strong interest with lipid management, hypertension, obesity, and lifestyle medicine Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Michelle Carpenter Contact Email: Michelle.Carpenter@vcuhealth.org Benefits: All VCU employees are eligible for a wide array of benefits to support you during your employment at VCU. Consult the benefits website for information on benefits eligibility according to employee type. Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 54cc1178 Last Name (required) 49cae7f7 Email (required) 633dd675 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-ou