    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/pulmonary-critical-care-medicine-pulmonary-hypertension-department-of-internal-medicine-m68069-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Pulmonary – Critical Care Medicine Pulmonary Hypertension | Department of Internal Medicine | M68069",
      "description": "Pulmonary – Critical Care Medicine Pulmonary Hypertension | Department of Internal Medicine | M68069 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Pulmonary – Critical Care Medicine Pulmonary Hypertension | Department of Internal Medicine | M68069 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Pulmonary – Critical Care Medicine Pulmonary Hypertension | Department of Internal Medicine | M68069 45001026 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Mission or goal of unit The mission of the Internal Medicine Department, Pulmonary Disease and Critical Care Medicine is to provide superior, compassionate, and innovative clinical care to our patients using state-of-the-art knowledge and resources and to conduct and disseminate clinical, research and scholarship, with a focus on the care of patients and education of future clinicians. Chief purpose of this position in support of above mission or goal The Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Pulmonary Disease and Critical Care Medicine is seeking to recruit and hire a qualified pulmonary and critical care physician interested in supporting the VCU Comprehensive Care Center for Pulmonary Hypertension, while expanding critical care and general pulmonology coverage. Duties & Responsibilities Teaching Although this position has no specific assigned teaching responsibilities, a successful candidate will be expected to integrate students and residents into clinical services provided. Research Although this position has no specific assigned research responsibilities, reasonable scholarly activities, such as publications, presentations at national meetings and participation in appropriate academic organizations, are expected. Service Work with institutional staff and administration to attain the strategic objectives of VCU Medical Center, including patient safety, patient and other customer satisfaction, maintenance and enhancement of public perception, and fiscal health Serves on institutional committees, study sections, review groups, as a journal editor, or editorial boards Clinical Primary clinical responsibilities will be to provide exemplary care in pulmonary disease and critical care medicine, to include support of the VCU Comprehensive Care Center for Pulmonary Hypertension, while expanding critical care and general pulmonology coverage. Outpatient Clinic/Outreach: The successful applicant will assist with outreach for our general pulmonary and pulmonary hypertension programs. Outreach involves expanding the outpatient clinic footprint of VCU Health and bringing in new patients to the Health System. Inpatient Critical Care Support: The successful candidate will aid in meeting our growing needs for critical care services and essential as we restructure critical care consultation services including night coverage, procedural and sedation services, staffing of new admissions to the ICU, supporting house-staff and the Advanced Practice Providers (APP) team thereby increasing critical care capacity Pulmonary Hypertension Consultation services Pulmonary Consultation services Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications M.D. or D.O. degree Successful completion of an ACGME-approved pulmonary and critical care fellowship Board Eligible - American Board of Internal Medicine, Pulmonary Medicine and Critical Care Medicine Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Board Certified - American Board of Internal Medicine, Pulmonary Medicine and Critical Care Medicine Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Brent Kimball Contact Email: Brent.Kimball@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 6a78b07f Last Name (required) 737519b3 Email (required) d2cf93ce Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 1842254f First Name (required) 801df333 Last Name (required) a68ffa83 Email (required) 97f307b9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Dou