      "title": "Urologist, Department Urology, Community Memorial Hospital (M67754)",
      "description": "Urologist, Department Urology, Community Memorial Hospital (M67754) - South Hill, Virginia, United States Urologist, Department Urology, Community Memorial Hospital (M67754) - South Hill, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Urologist, Department Urology, Community Memorial Hospital (M67754) 45000916 South Hill, Virginia, United States Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Urology Mission or Goal of Unit: The mission of the Department of Urology is the pursuit of excellence in all three areas of an academic surgical practice: teaching, research, and patient care. Chief Purpose of the Position: The Department of Urology is recruiting for an open rank, term, non-tenured track faculty position in the area of urology. The candidate will primarily provide clinical services at the CMH Campus located in South Hill, VA, to include clinic, operative services, and call coverage. Teaching The faculty member is expected to conduct resident grand rounds 1-2 times per year and attend via zoom 60% of the time. Research The faculty member is expected to participate in clinical trials as available. Service The faculty member is expected to serve on departmental and/or health system committees as necessary. Clinical The faculty member is expected to build and maintain a busy, patient centered clinical practice. This includes both inpatient and outpatient management of all general urological diagnoses and operative procedures. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Graduation from ACGME accredited residency Board Certification or Eligibility in Urology Superior communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level Experience in quality and education Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible : No Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Lisa Hook Contact Email: lisa.lomagliohook@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 21468106 Last Name (required) 8594ac35 Email (required) d37f0e39 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 2b9d21ee First Name (required) 5c9e798c Last Name (required) fd6dc6e2 Email (required) b0cbafee Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of