      "description": "Family Medicine Physician Williamsburg | Family Medicine | SOM | M67802 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Family Medicine Physician Williamsburg | Family Medicine | SOM | M67802 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Family Medicine Physician Williamsburg | Family Medicine | SOM | M67802 45000942 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Health Sciences MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Unit: School Of Medicine Department: Family Medicine This position is located at VCU Health Family Medicine at William & Mary - Williamsburg, VA Mission or Goal of Unit The VCU Department of Family Medicine and Population Health exists to: IMPROVE the health and well-being of the people of Virginia and beyond ADVANCE the science of epidemiology, family medicine, and public health by means of innovative, interdisciplinary research EDUCATE ourselves, our patients, our learners, and other stakeholders PROVIDE high quality primary care, public health services, and lead their integration TRAIN the next generation of epidemiologists, family physicians, and public health professionals Chief Purpose of this position The Department of Family Medicine and Population Health at Virginia Commonwealth University is currently recruiting for a BC/BE family physician at our This position is located at VCU Health Family Medicine at William & Mary in Williamsburg, VA. We are seeking a Full-Time physician that will be involved in medical student teaching and could participate in departmental research programs. This position will come with a competitive salary and generous benefit package as well as the ability to earn clinical bonuses. Position Responsibilities Provide the highest quality of primary care services to new and established patients in the community. Medical student teaching in a clinical setting Research and scholarly work according to training and interest Serve on hospital or departmental committees when appropriate. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board certified or board eligible in Family Medicine Eligible for full staff privileges at VCU Health System Eligible for medical licensure in Virginia Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Salary Range: Commensurate with experience Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Name: Ashley Krauss Contact Email: ashley.krauss@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 6d85f0e8 Last Name (required) 1bf7dc2c Email (required) 38458ea7 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: a09f40af First Name (required) 94156767 Last Name (required) 2d174671 Email (required) cf915a4f Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of