    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/director-of-evaluation-for-undergraduate-medical-education-ume-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Evaluation for Undergraduate Medical Education (UME)",
      "description": "Director of Evaluation for Undergraduate Medical Education (UME) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Director of Evaluation for Undergraduate Medical Education (UME) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director of Evaluation for Undergraduate Medical Education (UME) 45000720 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Medicine MBU Chief Purpose of this Position: This open rank faculty position as the Director of Evaluation for Undergraduate Medical Education (Director) provides strategic leadership and oversight of evaluation, data analytics, and scholarly inquiry to inform and advance undergraduate medical education (UME) at the Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine. This role is responsible for shaping the vision, strategy, and execution of the UME evaluation enterprise to ensure alignment with institutional priorities, accreditation standards, and best practices in medical education. The Director is a leader on the Office of Medical Education (OME) Evaluation Team, supervising Research Analyst(s), and collaborating closely with VCU SOM faculty, leadership, and partners to design, implement, and evaluate programs that drive continuous quality improvement, innovation, and scholarly productivity. This position is accountable for educational data governance, ensuring data accuracy, integrity, and compliance with institutional and regulatory standards. The Director develops and leads strategic initiatives in program evaluation, oversees the design and dissemination of evaluation tools, and guides the analysis and reporting of quantitative and qualitative data to inform decision-making at all levels of the SOM. In addition, the Director fosters a culture of scholarly inquiry, advancing the academic mission through research collaborations, publications, and presentations. Core Responsibilities: Strategic Leadership Provide strategic vision, leadership, and oversight of program evaluation and educational research for undergraduate medical education Supervise and mentor research analyst(s) ensuring high-quality execution of assigned activities Act as a content expert on educational data analytics and evaluation, advising other faculty, staff, and leadership on best practices and data-informed decision making Anticipate emerging data needs and proactively design solutions that leverage advanced analytics, predictive modeling, and visualization tools Anticipate challenges and proactively develop solutions to support the educational mission and advance the objectives of the Evaluation Team Collaborate with undergraduate medical education partners to facilitate the use of collected data to drive data-informed decision making to optimize the design and delivery of the MD program Serve on School of Medicine committees and workgroups as assigned/appointed Data Management Lead the development, implementation, and refinement of tools, and execution of evaluation plans by the Evaluation Team Oversee the development and ensure the quality of reports and complex visualizations (i.e., data dashboards) using a user centered agile approach, ensuring data presented is optimized for the intended audience Collaborate with leadership in the Office of Medical Education to review and respond to requests for data Establish and maintain data quality standards, including validation procedures and integration of multiple data sources Acts as a data steward for the School of Medicine, collaborating with School of Medicine Technology (SOMTech) partners, to manage data at all levels, including collection, preparation, storage, and analysis. Provide oversight for educational data governance, ensuring compliance with institutional policies and procedures, and state and federal regulations regarding the collection, maintenance, storage, and distribution of data Evaluation Lead the design, implementation, and refinement of program evaluation frameworks, models, and tools to guide ongoing program evaluation Collaborate with the Evaluation Team, OME leadership, and School of Medicine Leadership in the collection, analysis, and dissemination of evaluative data to support accreditation, curriculum review, and institutional decision-making as part of ongoing continuous quality improvement efforts Lead the advancement of evaluation processes by integrating best practices, national trends, emerging tools and technologies, and innovative approaches in UME Lead focus groups to support the collection of qualitative data Scholarly Activity Foster and lead scholarly activity in undergraduate medical education, including externally and internally funded research projects (i.e., data collection, data analysis, IRB submission) Promote dissemination of evaluation and research findings through peer-reviewed publications by collaborating with educational leaders and other faculty members across the School of Medicine and other VCU Schools and departments as may be applicable Conduct simple (i.e., descriptive) and complex data analyses (i.e., inferential statistics such as linear and logistic regression) as needed across projects Identify and pursue opportunities for grant funding and research partnerships to advance the educational mission of the School of Medicine Collaborate with the Director of Medical Student Research to design and deliver educational sessions to students to promote understanding and completion of medical education research activities Maintain compliance with all internal and external policies and processes regarding the completion of research and scholarly activities Advise on the design and execution of educational research projects Perform other duties as assigned Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications PhD, EdD, or other terminal degree in education, psychology, data science, or other related field with advanced training in research and evaluation methodology and statistics, or A minimum of three years of relevant work experience in program evaluation, designing and implementing research projects, analyzing data and creating report visualizations, preferably in health professions education Proficiency in both quantitative and qualitative research methodologies such as survey development, focus groups, interviewing, and data analysis Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines Excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills with the ability to effectively convey complex data to varied audiences Advanced knowledge of data management systems and statistical programs (e.g., SQL, tableau, Python, SPSS) Ability to work efficiently in a team environment in a collaborative manner providing subject matter expertise and support as needed Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience designing and/or refining dashboards and other tools to improve access to and display of data Experience managing and developing professional staff Experience in Undergraduate Medical Education (UME) or Health Professions Education, including familiarity with LCME accreditation processes Demonstrated record of scholarly productivity in medical education, including publications and presentations Proven ability to secure extramural funding in support of educational research and/or innovation Benefits: All full-time university faculty are eligible for VCU’s robust benefits package that includes comprehensive health benefits, paid annual and holiday leave granted up front, generous tuition benefits, retirement planning and savings options, tax-deferred annuity and cash match programs, employee discounts, well-being resources, abundant opportunities for career development and advancement, and more. Unit: School Of Medicine Department: Office of Medical Education Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted Position: No ORP Eligible Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Name: Katherine Mulloy Contact Email: kmulloy@vcu.edu Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 165806b3 Last Name (required) beb3f9bf Email (required) 52c9063c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 905c7900 First Name (required) 1fe7dfb9 Last Name (required) b56581de Email (required) 62c86d75 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs invites applications for a Senior Recruitment Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Academic Advising & Student Services, this position serves as the primary school-level point of contact for prospective students, faculty partners, and external partners interested in the L. Douglas Wilder School of Government and Public Affairs. This position drives student enrollment growth, elevates school visibility, and develops strategic recruitment and yield plans aligned with university enrollment strategies and the School’s academic priorities. The role provides strategic oversight for recruitment initiatives, market analysis, and pipeline development across community colleges and higher education institutions in the Mid-Atlantic region. The position directs graduate admissions operations, utilizes recruitment systems (Slate and Tableau), mobilizes faculty and staff engagement, collaborates closely with university leadership and graduate program directors, and leads a team dedicated to attracting a diverse, high-caliber student body. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 94169419 Last Name (required) 9674f517 Email (required) c69362aa Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along with third party non-persistent and persistent cookies to collect non-identifiable data from site visitors. VCU uses this collected data to prioritize and improve the content it delivers to its site visitors and to promote the university in a manner that is most relevant to its site visitors. I do not accept I accept"
