      "title": "Emergency Medicine Attending Physician - PRN- VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital - M89474",
      "description": "Emergency Medicine Attending Physician - PRN- VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital - M89474 - South Hill, Virginia, United States Emergency Medicine Attending Physician - PRN- VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital - M89474 - South Hill, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Emergency Medicine Attending Physician - PRN- VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital - M89474 45001275 South Hill, Virginia, United States Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Department: Emergency Medicine Chief Purpose of this Position: We are seeking an enthusiastic and dedicated individual to join our dynamic Emergency Medicine team as an hourly Emergency Medicine physician at our VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital in South Hill, VA. VCU Health Community Memorial Hospital sees 25,000 patients per year. The candidate will contribute to our mission of providing exceptional patient care and high-quality education in Emergency Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: Clinical - Provide excellent clinical care by demonstrating proficiency in the evaluation, diagnosis and management of a wide range of acute medical and traumatic conditions. Provide efficient, high-quality patient care that reflects current professional practice norms and skills and is consistent with accepted utilization guidelines. Quality/Safety - Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams to improve patient outcomes, participate in quality improvement initiatives, and promote patient safety and satisfaction. Administrative - Contribute to administrative and leadership responsibilities within the department, fostering a positive work environment and supporting the growth of Emergency Medicine services. Required Qualifications: Unrestricted Virginia Medical license or ability to qualify for one Board Certified/Board Eligible in Emergency Medicine; Fellowship training and/or additional subspecialty certification is desirable. Demonstrated a commitment to excellence in clinical care, education and research within the field of Emergency Medicine. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work effectively as part of a collaborative team. Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Salary Range: Commensurate ORP Eligible: No Contact Information: Contact Name: Sharlene Shannon Contact Email: sharlene.shannon@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 3498b2a4 Last Name (required) 1cf28459 Email (required) 4f908bb5 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: b4376208 First Name (required) 85a28ae1 Last Name (required) 18394bd6 Email (required) 60920507 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple