    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/general-pm-r-physician-m67772-m67773-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "General PM&R Physician (M67772 & M67773)",
      "description": "General PM&R Physician (M67772 & M67773) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States General PM&R Physician (M67772 & M67773) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search General PM&R Physician (M67772 & M67773) 45000927 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Unit: School Of Medicine Department: Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Mission or Goal of Unit: Our mission is to provide rehabilitation leadership to the Commonwealth of Virginia to improve the quality of life for individuals with disabilities by maximizing independence in living skills, recreation and employment activities through innovative education, evidence-based research, and outcome-focused patient care. Chief Purpose of this position: The Department of PM&R at VCU Health welcomes candidates to apply to this exciting new opportunity for a PM&R physician specializing in general outpatient practice. The advertised position is responsible for direct patient care, with opportunities to be involved in teaching, research, and service. A Physician Practice Group compensation plan provides an opportunity for a competitive, market-based salary. The position will be offered at an academic rank commensurate with qualifications. Teaching Assist in the supervision of residents, fellows, and other learners in the environment. Participate in the orientation of each group of house staff and students to the Rehabilitation program. Assist in establishing the core curriculum including a list of reading material for house staff and students. Assist in the evaluation of the house staff and students assigned to the facilities after each rotation. Research Though not a primary function of this job, participate as needed/interested in research activities as well as supporting ongoing and new projects as appropriate in the context of clinical care. Service Participate in university and department committees as requested. Contribute to the field of Physiatry overall through professional organizations. Clinical Primary clinical responsibility is general rehabilitation. Support established multi-specialty clinics in general PM&R diagnosis including, but not limited to, stroke, brain injury, spinal cord injury, and MSK. Responsible for the proper management and quality of service in the provision of care. Provide consults upon referral from medical facilities with formal coordinated relationships with the Department. Prepare periodic reports pertaining to the care of patients to the Division Chair. Ensure that medical services are documented and signed consistent with VCUHS and payer policies and guidelines. Assist in the establishment of referral sources for VCU Medical Center and Sheltering Arms Institute. Assist the billing professionals in the preparation of appropriate charges for the medical services rendered and in the review of non-reimbursed billings. Other Represent the Department in official meetings as requested. Attend scheduled Grand Rounds, staff conferences and lectures upon occasion as requested. Maintain practice credentials and completion of education as required by hospital, university, and state practice organization. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Medical Degree (MD or DO) Board certification in Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation Academic and clinical credentials that demonstrate ability to establish new clinical initiatives Effective oral and written communication Leadership skills Ability to work well with people in a team environment Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU. Salary Range: Commensurate Rank: Open Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Name: Rebecca Green Contact Email: rebecca.green@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 308cac50 Last Name (required) 707ed83a Email (required) 4bf8a270 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 5dad0ede First Name (required) afd3768d Last Name (required) fe19c3da Email (required) afbf5fa4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Senior Recruitment Coordinator VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The VCU L. Douglas Wilder School of Go