    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/english-adjunct-rolling-pool-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "English Adjunct (Rolling Pool)",
      "description": "English Adjunct (Rolling Pool) - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States English Adjunct (Rolling Pool) - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search English Adjunct (Rolling Pool) 45000838 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Adjunct College of Humanit and Sciences MBU Benefits : All VCU employee types are eligible for a wide array of benefits to support you during your employment at VCU. Consult the benefits website for information on benefits eligibility according to employee type. Unit: College of Humanit and Sciences MBU Department: English Duties & Responsibilities: The Virginia Commonwealth University College of Humanities and Sciences is recruiting a pool of adjunct faculty through June 30, 2026, for course sections within the English Department in the areas of Writing, Creative Writing, Linguistics, Literature and Film. This pool will be utilized on an as-needed basis. Your application will remain active until June 30, 2026; you may resubmit your application for subsequent years. Only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Position duties include: • Meet all designated course instruction guidelines. • Grade assignments and exams promptly based on instructions/rubric provided. • Respond to student inquiries within 24 hours. • Submit final grades according to College/Department policy Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in a related field with experience and specialized expertise directly related to the position. Demonstrated experience working in and fostering an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from various backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a member of VCU. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. or another doctoral degree in a related discipline or directly related to the position is highly preferred. Previous experience teaching courses within the Department of English curriculum. Demonstrated teaching experience. Candidates must apply online. Please include a Curriculum Vitae and contact information for two professional references. For information or questions about the position, contact Professor Sachi Shimomura, Associate Chair, at sshimomu@vcu.edu or Les Harrison at hlharrison@vcu.edu. Salary Range: $ 1,437 per credit hour FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 95e02cdc Last Name (required) 62d234d7 Email (required) a8523d54 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: f340a2c0 First Name (required) 1631436c Last Name (required) 24b4d1bf Email (required) 5b0793bd Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Digital Accessibility Administrator MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus MCV Main Campus. VCU Main Campus Unit: Office Of The Provost MBU Department: Academic Operations Duties & Responsibilities: Reporting to Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost and working closely with multiple campus partners, the Digital Accessibility Administra... Senior Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth Un