    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/endocrinology-physician-department-of-internal-medicine-m78513-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Endocrinology Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M78513",
      "description": "Endocrinology Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M78513 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Endocrinology Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M78513 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Endocrinology Physician | Department of Internal Medicine | M78513 45000974 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching Staff Endocrinology fellows’ clinic and endocrinology consultation service.Teach fellows, residents and medical students using adult teaching methods that enhance and encourage active learning and ongoing professional development. Complete students, residents and fellows evaluations. Participate in other endocrine educational activities including resident didactic series, noon conferences, morning report, Endocrine and Internal Medicine Grand Rounds, instruct undergraduate endocrine course and other educational duties assigned by the department and service. Research Participate in clinical and administrative research according to skills, interest and funding. Provide mentoring and supervision of fellows and residents in research and QI initiatives. Research opportunities may include performance improvement initiatives or formal extramurally funded investigations and participation may be as principle investigator or co-investigator. Service Work with institutional and administrative staff to attain the objectives of Virginia Commonwealth University and VCU Health System including patient safety, customer satisfaction, maintenance and enhancement of public perception and fiscal health. Clinical Provide excellent patient care in general endocrinology and focused areas of interest and experience in both inpatient and outpatient settings. Actively participate in management of patients on endocrinology consult service.Join colleagues in assuring service coverage 24/7/365. Other (for instance administrative duties, etc.) Comply promptly with billing, documentation, credentialing and other administrative requirements of the department. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board Eligible/Board Certified in Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism The candidate must qualify for an appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor level Demonstrated ability to work in and foster an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Salary Range: Commensurate ORP Eligible: No Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Shannon.Sekerak@vcuhealth.org Contact Email: Shannon.Sekerak@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 436a11a1 Last Name (required) 2671f9ff Email (required) 002a4683 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: fd29b4ed First Name (required) 09949869 Last Name (required) f91e5e29 Email (required) c4ef9dac Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Operations Manager of Survivorship and Palliative Care MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus We are seeking an Operations Manager of Survivorship and Palliative Care to help lead efforts to improve access, referral management, scheduling, clinic utilization, staffing coordination, patient flow, documentation processes, financial performance, and the patient and clinician experience. Senior Research Operations Manager Cancer Service Line Supportive Services MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus We are seeking a Senior Operations Research Manager who can provide senior-level operational leadership for the Cancer Service Line research portfolio, with primary support for survivorship, palliative care, cancer genetics, integrative health, food and nutrition initiatives, and external partnerships. Research Scientist & Tobacco Treatment Program Manager MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus We are seeking a motivated Research Scientist and Tobacco Treatment Program Manager to assist with developing and implementing rigorous survivorship research protocols, conducting epidemiologic and outcomes analyses, contributing to grants and publications, and translating findings into practical improvements in supportive oncology care. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current repor