      "title": "Hospitalist (Community Memorial Hospital) - South Hill, Virginia, United States",
      "description": "Hospitalist (Community Memorial Hospital) - South Hill, Virginia, United States - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Hospitalist (Community Memorial Hospital) - South Hill, Virginia, United States - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Hospitalist (Community Memorial Hospital) 45000866 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 South Hill, Virginia, United States Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: Schedule Hospitalists typically work a 7 on, 7 off model of 12-hour shifts. During the week, two physicians and two APPs round with a shift start time of 7 AM. Providers alternate in a round-and-go model with at least one provider staying until 7 PM. An admitter comes in a 10 AM and works until 10 PM. The night provider comes in at 7 PM and works until 7 AM. On the weekends, the admitter become a rounder, and there are no APPs and no admitter; the physicians admit in round robin fashion. Approximately one week in twelve is night coverage. Median census per physician team is 14 patients. Median number of day admissions is 8.5, and median number of night admissions is 6. Patient Load The patients are 100% inpatient with an open ICU. Median census per physician team is 14 patients. Median number of day admissions is 8.5, and median number of night admissions is 6. On-site consultation is available from pulmonary/critical care, cardiology, surgery, and anesthesia. Other consultation can be sought from subspecialists at VCU Medical Center in Richmond but may require the patient be transferred. Procedures Hospitalists rarely perform procedures, but comfort with central lines is preferred. Providers from surgery and anesthesia perform most procedures. Codes are run by hospitalists and emergency medicine providers. Teaching As part of the new family medicine residency in South Hill, physician will regularly supervise second- and third-year residents. Faculty are expected to provide typical supervision, train these residents on the care of adult inpatients, and complete evaluation and feedback of the residents. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible in Internal Medicine or Family Practice MD or DO degree Willingness to engage with the hospital and surrounding community to advance are in the region Desire to grow as a clinician and educator Demonstrated experience working in and fostering an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from various backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Salary Range: Commensurate FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Flexible Work Arrangement: Fully Onsite Rank: Open Contact Information: Contact Name: Amanda Marth | Associate Administrator Contact Email: Amanda.Marth1@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) ef792332 Last Name (required) b519ade2 Email (required) 83481f9e Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 9c59ee05 First Name (required) 364c11c4 Last Name (required) b74977a8 Email (required) 56ab5977 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Registered Nurse Manager, Supportive Oncology and Research Operations MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus We are seeking a registered nurse manager to support clinical coordination, personnel management, research and financial oversight. Clinical Research Coordinator/PATH Project Coordinator (*Restricted) MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus The VCU School of Nursing is seeking a Clinical Research Coordinator (CRC). The CRC is a specialized research professional who will work with and under the direction of the Principal Investigator (PI) to support the implementation and evaluation of the Partnership-based Approach to Translational Human-centered co-learning (PATH) project. Operations Manager of Survivorship and Palliative Care MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus We are seeking an Operations Manager of Survivorship and Palliative Care to help lead efforts to improve access, referral management, scheduling, clinic utilization, staffing coordination, patient flow, documentation processes, financial performance, and the patient and clinician experience. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) e40379c1 Last Name (required) 5942316a Email (required) 799d1040 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose of fulfilling form requests, so as you move through the web pages in that browsing session, the site will remember customized settings, choices made and content selected. These cookies are automatically discarded after closing the web browser. · Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies in order to provide improved services and enhance website performance. These cookies help VCU to count the number of visitors to VCU web pages, track visitor engagement on VCU web pages and improve the content VCU provides through its websites. These cookies are not automatically discarded upon browser closure. · Web Beacons and Third-Party Cookies: Some VCU official sites may use web beacons along with third party non-persistent and persistent cookies to collect non-identifiable data from site visitors. VCU uses this collected data to prioritize and improve the content it delivers to its site visitors and to promote the university in a manner that is most relevant to its site visitors. I do not accept I accept"
