    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/surgical-oncology-breast-cancer-research-department-of-surgery-som-f80620-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Surgical Oncology / Breast Cancer Research, Department of Surgery, SOM (F80620)",
      "description": "Surgical Oncology / Breast Cancer Research, Department of Surgery, SOM (F80620) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Surgical Oncology / Breast Cancer Research, Department of Surgery, SOM (F80620) - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Surgical Oncology / Breast Cancer Research, Department of Surgery, SOM (F80620) 45002567 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Teaching & Research Faculty School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Surgery Duties & Responsibilities: The Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) Department of Surgery, Division of Surgical Oncology, is seeking an accomplished and collaborative Teaching & Research (T&R) faculty member with expertise in breast cancer research to join its growing academic research enterprise. The successful candidate will establish and lead an externally funded, nationally recognized research program focused on clinically relevant questions in breast cancer and surgical oncology. The faculty member will be expected to develop an independent research portfolio, pursue sustained extramural funding, publish impactful peer-reviewed research, and contribute to the education and mentorship of medical students, residents, fellows, graduate students, and research trainees. This position is intended for a scientist with a strong record of research productivity and demonstrated potential for, or an established record of, extramural funding. The successful candidate will work closely with investigators and clinicians across the Department of Surgery, VCU Massey Comprehensive Cancer Center, VCU School of Medicine, and other university and health system partners to advance multidisciplinary breast cancer research. The faculty member will have opportunities to develop collaborative research programs spanning basic, translational, clinical, and/or population-based research, depending upon their area of expertise. Research and Scholarly Activity Establish, develop, and maintain an independent and externally funded research program focused on breast cancer, surgical oncology, or a closely related field Develop innovative research programs addressing clinically meaningful questions in breast cancer diagnosis, treatment, outcomes, prevention, survivorship, tumor biology, treatment resistance, health disparities, or related areas Prepare and submit competitive applications for federal, foundation, industry, and other extramural funding, including NIH and other national funding agencies. Develop and maintain a sustained portfolio of peer-reviewed publications in high-impact scientific and clinical journals Present research findings at national and international scientific and professional meetings Develop multidisciplinary collaborations with surgeons, medical and radiation oncologists, pathologists, radiologists, epidemiologists, bioinformaticians, population scientists, and other investigators Participate in the development of collaborative research initiatives within the Department of Surgery and VCU Massey Comprehensive Cancer Center Mentor research staff and trainees and contribute to the development of the next generation of breast cancer researchers Pursue opportunities for translational research and the implementation of research findings into clinical practice Participate in institutional research committees, scientific review activities, and other scholarly service appropriate to academic rank Collaboration and Institutional Engagement Establish collaborative relationships across VCU, VCU Health, Massey Comprehensive Cancer Center, and affiliated research institutions Contribute to multidisciplinary breast cancer research programs and disease-focused research initiatives Collaborate with investigators on interdisciplinary grants, clinical studies, translational research projects, and other scholarly initiatives Participate in Department of Surgery research programs, seminars, research-in-progress meetings, and other academic activities Support the growth of the Department's research enterprise through development of new research partnerships, funding opportunities, and scholarly programs Participate in institutional initiatives designed to expand the impact and visibility of breast cancer and surgical oncology research Education and Mentorship Mentor medical students, residents, fellows, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and research personnel Participate in graduate and medical education activities consistent with the faculty member's expertise and academic appointment Develop or contribute to research training opportunities for learners interested in surgical oncology and breast cancer research Provide mentorship in research methodology, scientific writing, grant development, and career development Participate in departmental and institutional educational conferences and seminars Clinical Collaboration While the primary focus of this position is research and scholarship, the faculty member will work closely with the Division of Surgical Oncology and multidisciplinary breast cancer teams to facilitate translation of research findings into clinical practice. Opportunities may include collaboration with clinical investigators in: Breast surgical oncology Clinical trials Translational research Cancer prevention and early detection Patient-reported outcomes and survivorship Health service research Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications PhD or equivalent terminal degree in biomedical sciences, cancer biology, molecular biology, genetics, immunology, biochemistry, or a related field Demonstrated research experience in breast cancer, breast disease, cancer biology, or a closely related area Evidence of scholarly productivity through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, or other scholarly contributions Demonstrated ability to conduct independent or collaborative research Experience with research methodologies appropriate to the candidate's area of expertise Demonstrated ability or potential to teach and mentor medical students, graduate students, residents, fellows, or other trainees Strong written and oral communication skills Ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary academic and research environment Preferred Qualifications Established research program focused on breast cancer or breast disease, including molecular, cellular, translational, clinical, population health, or outcomes research Strong record of peer-reviewed publications in breast cancer, oncology, cancer biology, or related fields Demonstrated success in obtaining or contributing to extramural research funding, including NIH, foundation, or other competitive funding Experience developing and leading investigator-initiated research projects Experience with translational research and/or collaboration with clinicians and multidisciplinary research teams Expertise in one or more relevant areas, such as: Breast cancer biology Tumor immunology Cancer genomics Molecular oncology Tumor microenvironment Cancer disparities Precision oncology Cancer prevention or survivorship Breast cancer outcomes or health services research Biomarker development Computational or data-driven cancer research Demonstrated record of teaching and curriculum development at the undergraduate, graduate, medical, or postgraduate level Salary Range: $101,000 - $115,000 Benefits : All VCU employee types are eligible for a wide array of benefits to support you during your employment at VCU. Consult the benefits website for information on benefits eligibility according to employee type. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Restricted: Yes ORP Eligible: Yes Rank: Open Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Mary Waite Contact Email: Mary.Waite@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 37b3ce91 Last Name (required) 710673a0 Email (required) 3c989756 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 66213bef First Name (required) 7c5d64dd Last Name (required) 8ef8c759 Email (required) 8aee2cf9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you (Rolling Pool) English Language Program Adjunct Instructor - Global Education Office VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The English Language Program (ELP) in the Global Education Office at Virginia Commonwealth University seeks qualified part-time adjunct faculty to teach in its intensive English language program. The ELP provides English language support to students who are academically admissible to VCU undergraduate and graduate programs but who need additional English language proficiency to succeed in an academic environment. The program also serves individuals seeking to improve their English language skills for educational, professional, and personal purposes, including prospective students who may later apply to VCU academic programs. Reporting to the Director of the English Language Program, adjunct faculty play an important role in supporting student language development and academic success while contributing to a welcoming and inclusive learning environment. Plastic, Reconstructive & Burn Surgery Research, Department of Surgery, SOM (F80610) MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Ticket Office Associate - Hourly VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus Ticket Office Assistants assist the full time ticket office staff in several key functions, including daily office procedures and game day functions. They assist with phone, window, and mail orders for all athletic ticketed events. They may work independently or as a member of a team. Ticket Office Assistants work under limited supervision, making complex decisions independently and referring unprecedented issues to an upper-level manager. They typically report directly to a supervisor. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 00c30929 Last Name (required) ededa771 Email (required) c11384ed Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time the browser requests a page from the server. The purpose of cookies is to identify users in order to prepare customized web pages for them and allow VCU to prioritize and improve the content delivered to its site visitors. The following types of cookies may be used on a VCU official site: · Non-Persistent Cookies: Some VCU official sites use non-persistent cookies for the purpose 