    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/ophthalmologist-glaucoma-fellow-ophthalmology-som-m89834-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Ophthalmologist: Glaucoma Fellow | Ophthalmology | SOM | M89834",
      "description": "Ophthalmologist: Glaucoma Fellow | Ophthalmology | SOM | M89834 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Ophthalmologist: Glaucoma Fellow | Ophthalmology | SOM | M89834 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Ophthalmologist: Glaucoma Fellow | Ophthalmology | SOM | M89834 45002617 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Ophthalmology Department Summary: The Glaucoma Fellowship at VCU Department of Ophthalmology provides advanced training in the full spectrum of glaucoma care, preparing fellows to become leaders in both clinical and surgical glaucoma management. Through a high-volume referral practice, the fellow will gain experience managing routine glaucoma cases as well as complex conditions. The fellow will receive robust surgical exposure and educational opportunities that support scholarly growth, professional development, and multidisciplinary collaboration. With personalized mentorship, state-of-the-art facilities, and a commitment to clinical excellence, the VCU Glaucoma Fellowship offers an exceptional training experience in a dynamic academic environment. The successful candidate must maintain high clinical and ethical standards that will be carried into decision-making processes, adhere to compliance measures, establish and promote an atmosphere of unity through collaborative practice and effective communication between all staff disciplines, and foster a high level of patient and staff satisfaction. Residents and certified ophthalmic medical technicians assist with patient care and ancillary testing. A Physician Practice Group compensation plan provides an opportunity for a competitive salary. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have successfully completed an ACGME-accredited ophthalmology residency program and be board certified or board eligible through the American Board of Ophthalmology. Candidates must also be eligible to obtain an unrestricted Virginia medical license and satisfy all institutional requirements for appointment to the VCU Health medical staff. Salary Range: Commensurate with experience FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Flexible Work Arrangement: Other Rank: Open Restricted : No Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Name: Brenda Ayala Contact Email: brenda.ayala@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 80b99c42 Last Name (required) 063ffb4a Email (required) 918abe67 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: c8db0465 First Name (required) 0e47480e Last Name (required) 11384d9e Email (required) 7dcd0819 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you (Rolling Pool) English Language Progr