      "description": "Optometrist |Ophthalmology | SOM | M89833 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Optometrist |Ophthalmology | SOM | M89833 - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Optometrist |Ophthalmology | SOM | M89833 45002616 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Ophthalmology Department Summary: The Department of Ophthalmology at the Virginia Commonwealth University Medical Center is seeking a residency-trained Optometrist with experience in contact lens fitting and ocular disease. As a member of our faculty, the successful candidate will be responsible for an established clinical practice with direct patient care in two outpatient settings including our Main Campus and our suburban satellite location. Our department supports a 12 resident ophthalmology training program with a full 5 year ACGME Accreditation. The successful candidate must maintain high clinical and ethical standards that will be carried into decision-making processes, adhere to compliance measures, establish and promote an atmosphere of unity through collaborative practice and effective communication between all staff disciplines, and foster a high level of patient and staff satisfaction. Residents and certified ophthalmic medical technicians assist with patient care and ancillary testing. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Candidate must have completed an Optometry Residency, with advanced training in Contact Lens Fitting and Ocular Disease. Candidate must also possess/maintain a current, full and unrestricted license to practice optometry in the State of Virginia. Salary Range: Commensurate with experience FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: No Flexible Work Arrangement: Other Rank: Open Restricted : No Tenure: Ineligible Months: 12 months Contact Name: Brenda Ayala Contact Email: brenda.ayala@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 00aaa814 Last Name (required) c552c02f Email (required) 2891f5c2 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 94cc3cb9 First Name (required) 5228add2 Last Name (required) 42466b4d Email (required) b34825bc Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you (Rolling Pool) English Language Program Adjunct Instructor - Global Education Office VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The English Language Program (ELP) in the Global Education Office at Virginia Commonwealth University seeks qualified part-time adjunct faculty to teach in its intensive English language program. The ELP provides English language support to students who are academically admissible to VCU undergraduate and graduate programs but who need additional English language proficiency to succeed in an