    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/department-of-internal-medicine-division-chief-of-cardiology-f73420-school-of-medicine-mcv-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Department of Internal Medicine | Division Chief of Cardiology | F73420 | School of Medicine",
      "description": "Department of Internal Medicine | Division Chief of Cardiology | F73420 | School of Medicine - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Department of Internal Medicine | Division Chief of Cardiology | F73420 | School of Medicine - MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Department of Internal Medicine | Division Chief of Cardiology | F73420 | School of Medicine 45001703 907 Floyd Avenue, MCV Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Clinical Faculty MCVP School Of Medicine MBU Advertising Summary: Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Unit: School Of Medicine MBU Department: Internal Medicine Duties & Responsibilities: Mission or Goal of Unit To provide superior, compassionate and innovative clinical care to our patients using state-of-the-art knowledge and resources and to conduct and disseminate clinical, research and scholarship, with a focus on the care of patients and education of future clinicians. Chief Purpose of this Position The Chief of the Division of Cardiology is responsible for leading and growing the clinical, education, research and advocacy missions surrounding the prevention and care of patients with cardiac disorders. The Division Chief will closely interact with the Director of the Pauley Heart Center as well as the Department of Internal Medicine. The Division includes faculty with interests in all areas of clinical cardiology; faculty members are located at Virginia Commonwealth University Medical Center, the Central VA Medical Center, Community Memorial Hospital and Tappahannock Hospital. Teaching In addition to overseeing the teaching activities of the division as a whole, the Division Chief will be expected to contribute to the teaching of medical students, residents, fellows and other healthcare professionals based on their expertise. Faculty routinely provide education with learners in their clinical sessions. In additional, the Chief will be expected to play a primary role in the mentoring of faculty in advancing their academic careers. Research The Chief should have a background in research with an established record of publication in high-impact journals. Success in securing external funding is preferred. They are expected to develop interdisciplinary collaborations to enhance the research program in the Department of Internal Medicine. The Division Chief encourages junior faculty, fellows and residents to participate in many ongoing basic, clinical and educational research projects. Faculty Affairs and Development: The Chief should provide strategic and operational leadership for faculty affairs, ensuring the recruitment, development, evaluation, and advancement of faculty in alignment with the missions of patient care, research, education, and service. In this role, the Chief will perform and oversee the annual faculty evaluation process, establishing performance expectations, assessing achievement of clinical, scholarly, educational, and administrative goals, and providing mentoring and feedback to support professional growth. The Chief will also be responsible for guiding and supporting faculty through the promotion and tenure process, ensuring that dossiers meet institutional and SOM standards and that faculty receive appropriate mentorship to achieve academic advancement. Additionally, the Chief should ensure adherence to the Division’s compensation plans for both Clinical Faculty and Teaching and Research Faculty, promoting transparency and accountability in compensation practices. This includes monitoring productivity and performance metrics and ensuring compliance with institutional policies and aligning compensation with individual contributions and the strategic objectives. Service The Chief will serve on departmental, College, and/or University and Hospital committees as necessary, as well as in a professional capacity in their field, e.g., reviewer, conference organizer, etc. Clinical Responsible for managing and growing the multidisciplinary team in the Cardiology Division which currently includes physicians, advanced practice providers, and pharmacist staffing clinic with responsibilities in the area of: Noninvasive and Preventative Cardiology Heart Failure Intervention Cardiology Electrophysiology Emergency Cardiology Services Atrial Fibrillation program Thoracic-Aortic Disease Program Mechanical Care Support Critical Care Congenital Heart Disease Cardio-oncology Cardiac imaging Other (for instance administrative duties, etc.) Management of day-to-day division operations, quality and safety, staffing, recruitment, budget, and division programs. This includes working with Department of Internal Medicine administration to promote the mission, vision, and goals of the division and department. The Division has satellite facilities in a number of locations in central Virginia which will also come under the leadership of the new Division Chief. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications M.D., or M.D./Ph.D. degree Board Certified in Internal Medicine and Cardiology Distinguished record of scholarship manifested by a strong publication record; should be nationally recognized for achievement in research Administrative leadership experience in an academic medical center Demonstrated experience working in and fostering an environment of respect, professionalism, and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from all backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a faculty member at VCU Preferred Qualifications Clinical and research expertise in academic cardiology Demonstrated ability to recruit and develop programs Record of scholarship, funding and research program development Track record of successful mentoring junior faculty Strong skills in medical education Experience with philanthropic fundraising and stewardship Salary Range: Commensurate Benefits : All VCU employee types are eligible for a wide array of benefits to support you during your employment at VCU. Consult the benefits website for information on benefits eligibility according to employee type. FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt ORP Eligible: Yes Restricted Position: No Sensitive Position: Yes Flexible Work Arrangement: Other Rank: Professor Tenure: Open Months: 12 months Contact Information: Contact Name: Dr. Todd Gehr Contact Email: Todd.Gehr@vcuhealth.org Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 4b6899e0 Last Name (required) aec56e37 Email (required) 1f6bf1a5 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 8f490704 First Name (required) f0762c8f Last Name (required) 56105b7d Email (required) 2e2fd66a Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you (Rolling Pool) English Language Program Adjunct Instructor - Global Education Office VCU Main Campus VCU Main Campus The English Language Program (ELP) in the Global Education Office at Virginia Commonwealth University seeks qualified part-time adjunct faculty to teach in its intensive English language program. The ELP provides English language support to students who are academically admissible to VCU undergraduate and graduate programs but who need additional English language proficiency to succeed in an academic environment. The program also serves individuals seeking to improve their English language skills for educational, professional, and personal purposes, including prospective students who may later apply to VCU academic programs. Reporting to the Director of the English Language Program, adjunct faculty play an important role in supporting student language development and academic success while contributing to a welcoming and inclusive learning environment. Plastic, Reconstructive & Burn Surgery Research, Department of Surgery, SOM (F80610) MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. Surgical Oncology / Breast Cancer Research, Department of Surgery, SOM (F80620) MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) a7f6bf03 Last Name (required) 9a993506 Email (required) 9144565e Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you! See you again soon. Close Candidate Details Use of Cookies A cookie is a small amount of data that is sent to your browser from a Web server and stored on the device you used to access the website. The cookie is then sent back to our server each time t