    "https://vcujobs.com/jobs/rolling-pool-english-language-program-adjunct-instructor-global-education-office-vcu-main-campus-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "(Rolling Pool) English Language Program Adjunct Instructor - Global Education Office",
      "description": "(Rolling Pool) English Language Program Adjunct Instructor - Global Education Office - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States (Rolling Pool) English Language Program Adjunct Instructor - Global Education Office - VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States Search Jobs Applicant Login Settings Kiosk mode Ready to join a workforce UN LIKE any other? Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search (Rolling Pool) English Language Program Adjunct Instructor - Global Education Office 45002735 907 Floyd Avenue, VCU Main Campus, Virginia, United States, 23284 Faculty Adjunct Global Education Office MBU The English Language Program (ELP) in the Global Education Office at Virginia Commonwealth University seeks qualified part-time adjunct faculty to teach in its intensive English language program. The ELP provides English language support to students who are academically admissible to VCU undergraduate and graduate programs but who need additional English language proficiency to succeed in an academic environment. The program also serves individuals seeking to improve their English language skills for educational, professional, and personal purposes, including prospective students who may later apply to VCU academic programs. Reporting to the Director of the English Language Program, adjunct faculty play an important role in supporting student language development and academic success while contributing to a welcoming and inclusive learning environment. Applicants will be considered on a rolling basis and based on program teaching needs. Responsibilities Teach one or more English language courses. Evaluate student performance and submit grades in accordance with program requirements. Hold scheduled office hours and meet with students as needed. Participate in program and team meetings. Foster a supportive and engaging classroom environment that promotes student learning and success. Required Qualifications Master's degree in TESOL or a related field, or a master's degree plus a TESOL certificate. Experience teaching English as a Second Language (ESL) at an accredited college or university. Demonstrated English language proficiency. Evidence of cross-cultural competence and sensitivity. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills. Demonstrated experience working in and fostering an environment of respect, professionalism and civility with a population of faculty, staff, and students from various backgrounds and experiences, or a commitment to do so as a member of the VCU community. Preferred Qualifications Two or more years of experience teaching in an intensive university ESL program in the United States. Experience teaching a variety of language skills and proficiency levels. Experience with language assessment, placement testing, or curriculum development. Technology proficiency relevant to language instruction. Position Details: Salary Range: $862 per ELP credit FLSA Exemption Status: Exempt Flexible Work Arrangement: 100% On-site Department: Global Education Office Rank: Instructor Benefits: VCU offers a comprehensive range of benefits and resources to support employees. Benefit eligibility varies by employee type. For additional information, please visit the VCU Benefits website . Apply now! Start by sharing your name and email, then proceed to the rest of your application. First Name (required) 442a89a2 Last Name (required) 4a67dbd7 Email (required) 4e850aa8 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thanks! We're looking forward to receiving your application soon. Send to someone else Submit information for your referral: 5d9143bf First Name (required) 3b35ef3b Last Name (required) 3cc070ae Email (required) 8002f891 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruiter outreach from Virginia Commonwealth University. You may opt-out at any time. Thank you for sharing this job! Recommended for you Postdoctoral Fellow MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus The Institute for Drug and Alcohol Studies (IDAS) at Virginia Commonwealth University invites driven doctoral-level researchers (Ph.D., M.D., Pharm.D., Psy.D., or equivalent) to apply for a Post-Doctoral Fellowship in Addictions Clinical Research. Working alongside NIH/NIDA-funded faculty in a multidisciplinary environment, you will lead high-impact human clinical trials, behavioral pharmacology studies, and advanced neuroimaging projects (fMRI/PET) while receiving hands-on, structured mentorship in grant writing (F32/K-series), manuscript publication, and trial design. Ideal candidates will possess a strong background in addiction science, clinical research methodology, and peer-reviewed publishing. This position offers access to up to $50,000 annually in educational debt relief through the NIH Extramural Loan Repayment Program (LRP). Senior HR Generalist MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. https://vcujobs.com/why-richmond Research Scientist - Microbiology and Immunology MCV Main Campus MCV Main Campus Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) School of Medicine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Richmond. Accounting for almost half of VCU’s sponsored research, the School of Medicine is internationally recognized for patient care and education. Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. EEO Virginia Commonwealth University is an equal opportunity employer. VCU Notice of Nondiscrimination Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal VCU's Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision Annual security and fire safety report Virginia Commonwealth University (VCU) is committed to assisting all members of the community in providing for their own safety and security. As required by federal law (The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, 20 U.S.C.1092(f), known as the “Clery Act”), the university publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, which contains information regarding campus security, crime reporting policies, personal safety and crime prevention, and fire and crime statistics for our various campus locations. To request a paper copy of the current report, please contact the VCU Police Department by calling (804) 828-3851 or in person at 224 E. Broad St., Richmond, Virginia 23219. E-verify Notice : After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Effective June 1, 2011, agencies in the Commonwealth of Virginia's Executive Branch will use the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. If you have questions or need accommodations during the application and interview process, please contact VCU Human Resources at (804) 828-0177 (Voice), (800) 828-1120 (TDD) or askhr@vcu.edu. The HR Welcome Center on the corner of Belvidere Street and W. Franklin Street is open Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Before you go... Let's keep in touch! First Name (required) 3dff426b Last Name (required) 85975321 Email (required) 2d692d24 Receive Job Alerts Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting contact information through this form, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive recruitment-related messages such as Job Alerts and recruit